{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations","id":941893,"title":"Geist 2nd Edition Thoughts & Speculations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-02T06:23:59-07:00","id":941893,"title":"Geist 2nd Edition Thoughts & Speculations","content":"With GenCon in the works, I know i'm thinking about the GenCon brochure forthcoming on Drivethrurpg, and what tid-bits it may give about the remaining Chronicles of Darkness lines yet to be given a 2nd edition: Geist &amp; Mummy. With mummy still publishing 1st edition materials, I think of the two, Geist is the most likely to be given a 2nd edition after Hunter (which is in the early stages of the works). So I thought i'd share some thoughts &amp; would love to hear some thoughts of potential mechanic/theme/ability changes. I loved the idea of Geist and enjoyed the 1st edition core, but it did feel like, with the old White wolf winding down, that the creators got a bit pressed for time and didn't get to flesh it out as much as they would like.<br /> <br /> A few folks have made some truly awesome Fan 1.5 GMC Geist pdfs here in this forum,<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/911888-my-1-5e-geist-updates\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/911888-my-1-5e-geist-updates\"> My 1.5E Geist Updates - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/911888-my-1-5e-geist-updates\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/911888-my-1-5e-geist-updates </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Greeting All, I drafted my ideas on how I would update Geist to be more in line with Second Edition, and I thought I would share with the community to get feedback. Here is the link (https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yLQSkr5n1EjjIePFcCX7B0gUFQtPiOgXetHTU1-hqGk/edit?usp=sharing). Comments in the document or here on the thread are both welcome. These updates focus for the most part on expanding the role of the Geist and updating Synergy. Like many people, I wanted to see the Geist given more focus and more of bite, but my preference is to keep the tone of Synergy as one of partnership and a </div> </div> </div><br /> Big shout out to both the link-makers here. Big fan <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Other folks pondering the possibility of a 2nd edition Geist, I totally recommend you taking a look at these creative insights.<br /> <br /> Perhaps this would be a Geist the Sin-Eater 2nd edition featuring the Abmortal Chronicle (always thought the abmortals were a good nemesis group for the Sin-Eaters, equally hard to kill antagonists who leave ghosts in their wake, wrecking havoc on the living &amp; the dead.)<br /> <br /> In Beast the Primordial, when the book discussed using the Integrity breaking points of other supernaturals to create more Lair chambers, there's a sidebar that specifically said a Werewolf's Harmony, a Demon's Cover, &amp; a Sin-Eater's Synergy wouldn't work for these purposes. To my mind, this implies that the SinEater/Geist relationship is similar to the give and take between Flesh &amp; Spirit in Werewolf 2E, with a middle score being preferable, a high score being too locked into the living world (difficult to use some manifestations, maybe control battles over the shared body like Johnny Blaze's Ghost Rider in the 70s?), and a low score being too locked into the Underworld (often getting trapped there or in Twilight, etc.).<br /> <br /> With the thematic link to Werewolf of Duality of Human &amp; Other (in this case ghost/shades rather than spirits), I imagine that the Ceremonial mystic rites of the Sin-Eaters would play a similar roll thematically (&amp; perhaps mechanically, but with a big shift in focus to death, ghost &amp; perhaps shadow control) to the 2E Werewolf's Spirit Rites. <br /> <br /> The Thresholds I see as retaining their names and basic themes &amp; Keys, though perhaps with Demon the Descent style Chthonic Beat (as opposed to an Arcane Beast from Mage) &amp; resolution added in.<br /> <br /> The Archetypes seem like they'd fit 2nd Edition mechanics better as Anchors (like a Vampire's Requiem &amp; Dirge, or a Werewolf's Blood &amp; Bone, or a Mage/Human's Virtue &amp; Vice), perhaps something like a Carneval (outward funeral, playing off the New Orleans &quot;krewe' link of the jazz parade tradition there, a &quot;farewell to the Flesh&quot;: remembering the past life of a Sin-Eater - bone-picker/materialist, etc) &amp; a Memorial (quiet, private funeral for the current, private person they are after the Bargain, their view of this second life - Celebrant, Pilgrim, Mourner etc.), &amp; as suggested by a few on Geist forums, perhaps a third for the Geist?<br /> <br /> To replace the Archetypes as a Social/Philosophical Splat, I would imagine something along the lines of a focus or duty held by members, but still having the loose connection between members that 1E Archetypes had. Examples being possibly some from the original Archetypes: Gatekeeper/Exorcist to maintain the balance &amp; spaces of the living &amp; the dead; Advocate to seek justice &amp; peace for those that can't get it themselves, often the dead; Reaper/Fury to send those living, dead or otherwise off to the next world that can't be stopped otherwise; (new but related to old Necromancer archetype) Oracle/Mystic to gaze into the Underworld and the wider World/Chronicle of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Geist has been incredibly unique among 1st edition CofD games in its supernatural powers (Manifestations/Key) structure. With 2nd edition making each game's abilities (Disciplines, Gifts, Arcana, Atavisms, Embeds, &amp; forthcoming: Transmutations, Contracts, Endowments) more unique systems than just a standard 5 dot within each sub power system, I'm interested to see what happens. <br /> Will Manifestations become basic abilities all Sin-Eaters have in a default mode &amp; the Key becomes the game ability (allowing the Geist to modify a basic ability for a scene)?<br /> Will the Elemental keys (given the move away from 1st edition's decision to give most supernaturals after Werewolf some measure of mental, elemental or animal control power -granted, very thematically appropriate for Changeling; but it has been specifically said by the Promethean 2E team leader that their powers have dropped the mental &amp; animal control entirely to focus on the themes of alchemy &amp; transmutation) be combined into a single elemental key (similar to Werewolf 2E's Elemental gifts), or removed, or be Threshold specific? <br /> Will there be Threshold specific Manifestations as well as Threshold preferred Keys?<br /> Will the Keys see a similar overhaul as Werewolf's Gifts &amp; Changeling's Contracts have? (only a few inherent splat ones in 5 dots and the rest more based on some characteristic of the Geist or Synergy? OR all Keys having a dot rating 1-5, but only loosely connected to each other into theme groupings, not in a step-by-step power acquisition procedure? OR something else entirely? Maybe<br /> Will the Caul become a standard, customizable ability, like the Demonic Form of Demon the Descent? Or perhaps the Geist gets cumstomized, and the Caul or other Manifestations allow the Geist's abilities to be used in 'human' form?<br /> <br /> And (last one I promise. Sorry for being longwinded, been thinking on this for months) will there be a companion splat this time around? something comparable to a 2nd Edition Ghoul, Wolf-Blooded, Sleepwalker/Proximi, Fae-Touched, or Stigmatic? With Geist sharing the duality theme of human and other (like Changeling &amp; the Fae), would it be reasonable for a Fae-Touched like individual (a natural medium, someone who clinically died, touched the underworld, but came back without a Geist bargain) to hold a piece of the Underworld's darkness in their soul and perhaps have a threshold based on their 'death' (like the fae-touched have a Seeming), granting them a Key and maybe one manifestation? These would be Orpheus, plural Orpheoi? (the mythology one, not the Classice WoD one, though there's a shared idea there of the living descending into the Underworld) style humans, who delve into the Underworld, but are not part of it to the extent of a Sin-Eater, lacking a Geist bond. Other names I could imagine for this possible character type would be: Ghost Walkers, Shade-Souled<br /> <br /> Please share your thoughts on these thoughts &amp; some thoughts of your own <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T16:04:33-07:00","id":942299,"title":"","content":"Remember that the &quot;[thing] Chronicle&quot; is more about something that defines the line than just being a threat; Mage was the Fallen World Chronicle and Promethean was the Firestorm Chronicle. <br /> <br /> Ideally, a Geist 2e would be built along the lines of a Krewe Chronicle, with more effort put into building your krewe's mythology and growing together as you all increase in power and understanding of death. My old group had the headcanon that Tier 3 krewes ascend beyond our reality to fundamentally alter the nature of the Underworld, and while that idea need not be stolen, I love the concept of doing archaeology on the krewes that have come before. Give the Twilight Network more legs and toss some example krewes out there, as Sin-Eaters seem to communicate with each other much more than the original book suggested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T16:25:06-07:00","id":942313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=942299#post942299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that the &quot;[thing] Chronicle&quot; is more about something that defines the line than just being a threat; Mage was the Fallen World Chronicle and Promethean was the Firestorm Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Ideally, a Geist 2e would be built along the lines of a Krewe Chronicle, with more effort put into building your krewe's mythology and growing together as you all increase in power and understanding of death. My old group had the headcanon that Tier 3 krewes ascend beyond our reality to fundamentally alter the nature of the Underworld, and while that idea need not be stolen, I love the concept of doing archaeology on the krewes that have come before. Give the Twilight Network more legs and toss some example krewes out there, as Sin-Eaters seem to communicate with each other much more than the original book suggested.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the Thoughts! A fair point. I got stuck in the idea of enemy or threat rather than defining the line. Giving the Twilight Network more attention and build up would definitely emphasize the Sin-Eaters' ability to communicate &amp; coordinate, despite having no set number of Vampire style covenants or Werewolf style tribes. I rather like the sound of a Twilight Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T13:18:51-07:00","id":944492,"title":"","content":"Heard on another Geist thread that Geist 2nd Edition has been confirmed!!!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> anyone seen a GenCon Aug 2016 Onyxpath brochure?????","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T15:16:31-07:00","id":944553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=944492#post944492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heard on another Geist thread that Geist 2nd Edition has been confirmed!!!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> anyone seen a GenCon Aug 2016 Onyxpath brochure?????</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know why, but I think someone may be excited. That said, I'm now a hypocrite, as I'm really excited too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T17:52:35-07:00","id":944619,"title":"","content":"Please please please bring back Shadowguiding for the Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T18:32:49-07:00","id":944636,"title":"","content":"Please ignore the people trying to turn Geist into Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T18:46:35-07:00","id":944641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=944636#post944636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please ignore the people trying to turn Geist into Wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing wrong with having someone else at the table play the alien voice in your head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T19:01:45-07:00","id":944650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=944641#post944641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's nothing wrong with having someone else at the table play the alien voice in your head.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is to some people.<br /> <br /> Many people would prefer to roleplay their own geist rather than another player having so much control over such a major aspect of their character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T19:35:51-07:00","id":944666,"title":"","content":"It can be an optional, you know, like a whole ton of other subsystems and rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T21:33:57-07:00","id":944691,"title":"","content":"I remember reading a few put together changes in one of the more recent books, general advice such as reducing the damage from Rage by 1 or the Shroud's armor bonus. However, I just can't find it in the books I have (could have sworn it was in Beast). Do you guys a) know what I'm talking about, so I know I'm not crazy, or b) think that they'll be implemented into the game proper?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T00:16:51-07:00","id":944744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=944691#post944691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading a few put together changes in one of the more recent books, general advice such as reducing the damage from Rage by 1 or the Shroud's armor bonus. However, I just can't find it in the books I have (could have sworn it was in Beast). Do you guys a) know what I'm talking about, so I know I'm not crazy, or b) think that they'll be implemented into the game proper?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast has a section for converting unconverted gamelines to 2e, and as part of it, it says that attack modifiers and ballistic armour ratings should be reduced by one. So that's probably what you're thinking of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">It can be an optional, you know, like a whole ton of other subsystems and rules.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">If it's an optional rule, that's fine. It's just that if it's a default rule it creates a rather different atmosphere and requires a lot more work and I know many people dislike having one of the biggest aspects of their roleplaying and character concept taken away from them.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 08-06-2016, 03:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T00:40:31-07:00","id":944748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=944744#post944744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast has a section for converting unconverted gamelines to 2e, and as part of it, it says that attack modifiers and ballistic armour ratings should be reduced by one. So that's probably what you're thinking of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many thanks; I guess I just mis-remembered a more detailed list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T06:41:34-07:00","id":944813,"title":"","content":"Now that it's officially on the table (pardon the tabletop pun), is anyone else itching to be a playtester or to submit samples of writing (in my case amateur writing)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T08:21:16-07:00","id":944856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=944666#post944666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can be an optional, you know, like a whole ton of other subsystems and rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of a subsystem would that need? It seems to me that all it would require would be for the Storyteller to say, &quot;Okay, each of you controls the Geist of another character.&quot; That said, I would be fine with it if the rule was optional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T09:11:20-07:00","id":944884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=944744#post944744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">If it's an optional rule, that's fine. It's just that if it's a default rule it creates a rather different atmosphere and requires a lot more work and I know many people dislike having one of the biggest aspects of their roleplaying and character concept taken away from them.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think there's room in RPG-land for a co-op game that shakes things up. But I'm an old curmudgeon so what do I know?<br /> <br /> Still hoping for an honest-to-god CoD Wraith to make it into print (or for OPP to admit they won't do it so the fans can fully take it over).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T10:25:07-07:00","id":944928,"title":"","content":"I am hoping they make Charm creation a bit more intuitive. Certain Charms in the book's samples (such as the the Bus Ticket) seem to have conditional abilities (a free bus fare that you get back) but the text doesn't support it. It is confusing for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T10:28:45-07:00","id":944932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=944928#post944928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am hoping they make Charm creation a bit more intuitive. Certain Charms in the book's samples (such as the the Bus Ticket) seem to have conditional abilities (a free bus fare that you get back) but the text doesn't support it. It is confusing for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second this, although I also hope that they don't sacrifice the atmospheric-ness of Charms, Memorabilia etc for the sake of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T17:04:14-07:00","id":945159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=942299#post942299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that the &quot;[thing] Chronicle&quot; is more about something that defines the line than just being a threat; Mage was the Fallen World Chronicle and Promethean was the Firestorm Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Ideally, a Geist 2e would be built along the lines of a Krewe Chronicle, with more effort put into building your krewe's mythology and growing together as you all increase in power and understanding of death. My old group had the headcanon that Tier 3 krewes ascend beyond our reality to fundamentally alter the nature of the Underworld, and while that idea need not be stolen, I love the concept of doing archaeology on the krewes that have come before. Give the Twilight Network more legs and toss some example krewes out there, as Sin-Eaters seem to communicate with each other much more than the original book suggested.</div> </div> </div> </div>personally, I don't think that Geist's 2nd edition would feature something like &quot;Krewe Chronicles&quot;. I don't mean that there shouldn't be a lot of emphasis on krewes in 2e- there should- but usually, the &quot;X Chronicles&quot; thing is something which both clash and reinforces the themes of the gameline. Each splat has a tendency to circle around a certain refuge from the darkness- until something force it back in, showing that there is nowhere to horror of the world. Vampires play sophisticated political games against each other, when a strix come and break all the rules. Werewolves hunt as they must, when an enemy which is not recognized by their old traditions rise and being chaos to both flesh and spirit. A mage is busy in her occult research and is on the verge of a breakthrough- when her magical senses starts tingling, and they won't let go until she'll investigate the new mystery. A promethean is in the middle of his pilgrim when the Fire descends and the world change, forcing him to change with it. Changelings manage to re-create their small place in the world, until a huntsman come and tries to drag her back to a mad story of beautiful madness. Hunters follow a series of cruel killings, and as they expect to find a monster they find a person- crazy and twisted, but still a person. Even regular people, who are just on their way to live their small and regular life, may stumble upon a strange machinery, and since that moment their life just won't be the same.<br /> <br /> Each game has a story to tell, and the featured Chronicle is meant to help you tell it- it shakes things up and change the status que, throwing the characters into a situation not well understood and which could change everything in their small corner of the world. Suddenly, vampires are reminded of their own personal horror, werewolves discover why they must hunt, mages discover the price of their own hubris in search for truth...<br /> <br /> the question we need to ask is this- what would make a sin eater remember that it is a game about Second Chances?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T17:58:09-07:00","id":945190,"title":"","content":"Part of me thinks that it should be the Averian Chronicles or the Cthonic Chronicles where the underworld periodically tries to drag the geist back into the underworld with you either still attached or dead, but where it's easier to resist the underworld and it's machinations when you've got a combination of memorbilia and krewe to anchor yourself to. I also think that memorbilia should be more personal, be sort of ghost-y anchors but for you. Be things important to the sin-eater that have been infused with cthonic energies and tied to people the sin-eater has lost, rather than just dead-related stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T18:19:43-07:00","id":945199,"title":"","content":"I just want krewes to take center stage because they seem at least as vital to Sin-Eaters as packs are to Werewolves and possibly even more so, what with the whole building your mythology thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T20:18:12-07:00","id":945249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=945199#post945199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want krewes to take center stage because they seem at least as vital to Sin-Eaters as packs are to Werewolves and possibly even more so, what with the whole building your mythology thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do hope they clean up the mythology thing. It's abit weird that the geist can have one theme before you join a krewe and then once you join a krewe it might suddenly become completely different. I don't think it was explained well in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T00:10:59-07:00","id":945329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=945249#post945249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do hope they clean up the mythology thing. It's abit weird that the geist can have one theme before you join a krewe and then once you join a krewe it might suddenly become completely different. I don't think it was explained well in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. I always find this really difficult to use in any significant fashion in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T00:14:20-07:00","id":945332,"title":"","content":"I'm also quite curious about how the Manifestations are going to be arranged, given 2e's thing so far about moving away from the linear 1-2-3-4-5 type powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T00:23:12-07:00","id":945337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=945332#post945332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also quite curious about how the Manifestations are going to be arranged, given 2e's thing so far about moving away from the linear 1-2-3-4-5 type powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually something I hope they keep the same. Geist was the only game of the line that had a quadratic power set - any key gained would exponentially increase the number of manifestations you had available, and any manifestation gained meant you had even more powers to your already existing keyset. Really, changing the system now would seem like a nerf, when virtually all the updated gamelines seem to have granted buffs. The powers themselves could be updated, particularly so they fit in with the new rule set, but changing the powerset overall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T00:34:43-07:00","id":945345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=945337#post945337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is actually something I hope they keep the same. Geist was the only game of the line that had a quadratic power set - any key gained would exponentially increase the number of manifestations you had available, and any manifestation gained meant you had even more powers to your already existing keyset. Really, changing the system now would seem like a nerf, when virtually all the updated gamelines seem to have granted buffs. The powers themselves could be updated, particularly so they fit in with the new rule set, but changing the powerset overall?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to see a couple new Manifestations (perhaps along the lines of the fan-made Hearse) and Keys, but I can agree with you that I think that the system would work, although the powers themselves could have had a bit more care put into their placement and relative power level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T23:20:26-07:00","id":946764,"title":"","content":"Something else I'd like to see is some changes to Ceremonnies. Less the Ceremonies themselves, which I think are extremely atmospheric, but more to uncouple them from merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:21:48-07:00","id":947052,"title":"","content":"Personally, the concept of Krewes as described in 1e never really grabbed me. For one, I agree with the general consensus that the mythology aspect was just... weird. For being the splat's equivalent to Court, Covenant, Order, etc. it felt... tacked on. Like instead of developing even a general Sin-Eater society, the book just left it up to the players. I mean, that's not a terrible idea in and of itself. A system for creating your own organizations along the lines of a Covenant with knobs and levers to build the benefits thereof based on the group's common beliefs would make for a great <i>supplement</i>, but it just felt odd and out of place in Geist. I mean, I know such a subsystem must have taken a lot of time and effort to build, but its inclusion as a core part of the game, to me, came off as, &quot;We didn't have time/interest in building a 'Sin-Eater Culture.' Here, you do it.&quot; I'm sure that's not the intent, just what it felt like to me. It felt like getting a Vampire core book, and in the section about Covenants it saying, &quot;Vampires often organize into sociopolitical factions based on common ideals, goals, and mythology. We're not going to give you any examples of what those are or how they interact with each other. That's for you to do. Thanks for paying for this non-content!&quot;<br /> <br /> Again, I know that couldn't have been the intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T13:51:08-07:00","id":947205,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, something that I would very much like to see (and this might just be the ritual magic fanatic in me talking) is a system for creating Ceremonies, both because I personally like them and shamelessly abuse them whenever I can (both as a player and ST) and because I feel that Sin-Eaters as a group are generally not the kind of people to endlessly re-use the ceremonies of the preceding generations. Perhaps there could be a Merit (or perhaps a separate Advantage) that, instead of giving single, specific ceremonies, gave a character the ability to create ceremonies of a certain power, scaling upwards as more dots are purchased. Perhaps Ceremonies could be based off of or incorporate the user's Manifestations, being a method of amplifying and focusing the deathly power of the geist and the Underworld more precisely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T21:05:32-07:00","id":947464,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Create a Court&quot; for changeling 2e has been brilliant. So &quot;Create a Krewe&quot; could work if it was handled better. Part of me wants more focus towards the roles krewemates are meant to have, without it just becoming like WtF.<br /> <br /> As for Ceremonies, I'd rather than not be as freeform as ajf115's suggestion sounds like it would end up as. Though I definitely want ceremonies to be more customisable in how they are actually performed, without increasing the experience cost of the ceremony. Updating a ceremony should be the default assumption so it fits the time, culture, personalities of the krewe and it's geists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 08-10-2016, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T23:31:17-07:00","id":947561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=947464#post947464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &amp;quot;Create a Court&amp;quot; for changeling 2e has been brilliant. So &amp;quot;Create a Krewe&amp;quot; could work if it was handled better. Part of me wants more focus towards the roles krewemates are meant to have, without it just becoming like WtF.<br /> <br /> As for Ceremonies, I'd rather than not be as freeform as ajf115's suggestion sounds like it would end up as. Though I definitely want ceremonies to be more customisable in how they are actually performed, without increasing the experience cost of the ceremony. Updating a ceremony should be the default assumption so it fits the time, culture, personalities of the krewe and it's geists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I was probably not very clear. I'd like there to be plenty of pre-made ceremonies that you can use without making any changes, I'd just like the rules to be there for making new ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T01:16:06-07:00","id":947599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=947561#post947561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I was probably not very clear. I'd like there to be plenty of pre-made ceremonies that you can use without making any changes, I'd just like the rules to be there for making new ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yeah that sounds useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T10:50:38-07:00","id":947873,"title":"","content":"Maybe make it so there's the default Ceremonies, but you can develop new ones that are tied to your Krewe's symbolism?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T11:01:16-07:00","id":947883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=947873#post947873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe make it so there's the default Ceremonies, but you can develop new ones that are tied to your Krewe's symbolism?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like that, or ones connected to your geist's nature (as expressed through their Keys).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T19:13:43-07:00","id":948263,"title":"","content":"My biggest hope is that they don't fuck up the theme.<br /> <br /> Everygame after the big three has something, mechanical or thematic, that makes it a bit distinct from the big three.<br /> <br /> Promeathean is a lot suckier than most splats, but you can get your happy ending, the rules for it are right in the book, for example. Vampire, Mage, and Werewolf don't have built in happy endings.<br /> <br /> Geist's theme was Accepting Death and that the world is dark, but that there was genuinely good stuff too and that Life was worth celebrating. It is upbeat, it is happy. Likewise, being a Sin-Eater usually doesn't suck. The Sin-Eater Template has no major drawbacks. You were dead, now you're not and as an added bonus you have powerful psychic abilities and a head guest that has it in their best interests to keep you alive and happy. That's awesome.<br /> <br /> Yeah, there are cases of a a particularly weak willed Sin-Eater being bullied into compliance by their geist, or particularly inhuman geists driving hosts insane, but that's always presented as an NPC. It's not the default, it's either an NPC or it's a <i>Player</i> opting into it with their PC because they think it will be fun or interesting. Also, yeah, if you died too many times you were either driven insane, became a meat puppet, or just stayed dead, but you're not starting there, you get there by screwing up a lot. The default assumption is that either the Sin-Eater is mostly in control or that both host and geist are equal partners.<br /> <br /> Being a Sin-Eater does <b>not </b>suck. Please keep it that way, because that makes Geist distinct from both Wraith and from the rest of the CroD, because no inherent drawbacks Every other splat has at least 1(except Hunters, but they hardly count).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T17:55:31-07:00","id":950822,"title":"","content":"I apologize for the double post, but since it's been a few days...<br /> <br /> I'd kind of it if Mementos, not just charms but all of them, got an entire chapter to themselves explaining them with plenty of examples of every kind.<br /> <br /> and maybe more than one kind per each dot ranking,<br /> <br /> In particular, there are lots of famous and infamous dead people. There could be an entire supplement that's just fully of Memorabilia examples. Throw in rumors about these people and their deaths...<br /> <br /> ...Damn it, now I want to play a Necromancer who has &quot;Hitler's one ball&quot; in a jar and uses it in his ceremonies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:33:31-07:00","id":952033,"title":"","content":"Sineaters do have a massive down side, every time they die after the first time, someone dies in your place, so someone kills you, but you come back only to find out your young daughter has died because you came back. That's a huge burden of guilt to bear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:38:03-07:00","id":952037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=952033#post952033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sineaters do have a massive down side, every time they die after the first time, someone dies in your place, so someone kills you, but you come back only to find out your young daughter has died because you came back. That's a huge burden of guilt to bear.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, though, that kind of guilt doesn't have the same mechanical weight as Promethean's Disquiet and Wasteland or Vampire's 'you go in the sun and you die' shtick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:25:29-07:00","id":952081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=952033#post952033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sineaters do have a massive down side, every time they die after the first time, someone dies in your place, so someone kills you, but you come back only to find out your young daughter has died because you came back. That's a huge burden of guilt to bear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, probably not your daughter. It's a random person, making it unlikely for it to be anyone you know, let alone someone close to you. Still distressing to cause an innocent's death of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:38:48-07:00","id":952094,"title":"","content":"Though it could be refocused in 2E to make it more immediately relevant to the Sin-Eater in question. If a Requiem 2E like Touchstone system is used, they might even drop the &quot;lose 2 from Max Synergy&quot; cost for resurrection... all for the low, low price of one of your Touchstones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T20:33:19-07:00","id":952251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=952094#post952094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though it could be refocused in 2E to make it more immediately relevant to the Sin-Eater in question. If a Requiem 2E like Touchstone system is used, they might even drop the &amp;quot;lose 2 from Max Synergy&amp;quot; cost for resurrection... all for the low, low price of one of your Touchstones.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is deliciously evil. But what about non-human or non-living Touchstones? They can't die in a Threshold thematic way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T23:26:41-07:00","id":952347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=952251#post952251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is deliciously evil. But what about non-human or non-living Touchstones? They can't die in a Threshold thematic way.</div> </div> </div> </div>You return to life with the vision of your grave destroyed or otherwise desecrated.<br /> You return to life with a vision that the tranquil spot in the forest where you surround yourself in life's beauty is being ravaged by a bushfire.<br /> You return to life with a vision of an obscured figure tearing into the portrait of your dead lover. <br /> <br /> Though personally, I'd rather the touchstones be things that reminds the Geist of their life. Helping them be a dead soul with links to life rather than just the sin-eater being a living individual with links to death. Alternatively, embrace the Persona inspiration and go Social Links and have touchstones make you more powerful in some minor way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 08-17-2016, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T07:54:14-07:00","id":952514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=952347#post952347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You return to life with the vision of your grave destroyed or otherwise desecrated.<br /> You return to life with a vision that the tranquil spot in the forest where you surround yourself in life's beauty is being ravaged by a bushfire.<br /> You return to life with a vision of an obscured figure tearing into the portrait of your dead lover.<br /> <br /> Though personally, I'd rather the touchstones be things that reminds the Geist of their life. Helping them be a dead soul with links to life rather than just the sin-eater being a living individual with links to death. Alternatively, embrace the Persona inspiration and go Social Links and have touchstones make you more powerful in some minor way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not both? The living Sin-Eater has their Touchstones, and the Geist has theirs. Losing either is likely to eventually make your Synergy shaky, since the Sin-Eater has less ties to the living world, and the Geist becomes more inhuman.<br /> <br /> Why would a Geist tank one of their own Touchstones to raise the Sin-Eater? Because this partnership is <i>important</i>, damn it!<br /> <br /> They could either be handled the same, or treated differently for some systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T20:26:24-07:00","id":953622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=952033#post952033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sineaters do have a massive down side, every time they die after the first time, someone dies in your place, so someone kills you, but you come back only to find out your young daughter has died because you came back. That's a huge burden of guilt to bear.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not an inherent downside. That's punishing you for screwing up, and depending on the character it's not even that big a punishment. The loss of synergy is, but that should probably go because &quot;I brought you back to life, now we permanently can't have as good a relationship as before&quot; makes no sense.<br /> <br /> A Major inherent Drawback is something like having a random change to fly into a murderous rage, or not being able to go out in daylight because the sun will kill you. Or literally the whole world hating you. Or your powers not working right if you try to go flashy. Stuff that makes just existing hard. Stuff you have a legitimate reason to angst over, stuff that was forced on you.<br /> <br /> The biggest downside to being a Sin-Eater, unless you're one of the edge cases, is that ghosts know that you can see them and the more lucid ones <i>might </i>bug you about solving their issues. There are ceremonies that can make them leave you alone.<br /> <br /> The lack of supernatural angst is a feature, not a bug. Don't fuck with it, that's the appeal. &quot;You made a deal. The person making the deal is so desperate that the deal is stacked heavily in your favor. You don't die and you get awesome powers. In exchange, your head guest would like it if you occasionally do things for it, and you're totally allowed to tell it to shut up and think of something else if you don't want to do what it asked you to do.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> and Milo V3: Or we could not make the game angstier and thus remove one of it's selling points?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 08-18-2016, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T21:22:57-07:00","id":953653,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest downside of being a Sin Eater is the Geist themselves; one of the sample adventures, Dem Bones, had the titular Geist repeat the same bar of a particular song over and over again, to the point his Sin Eater was using suicide just to get any sleep. Geists can be nice, they can be scary, and then they can crack your sanity. Don't forget they also mess with your vision at times too.<br /> <br /> But yeah, overall Sin Eaters lack a lot of the angst that other splats have, and I agree, it's a great feature. As a trade-off, while they're very hard to kill, they're not exactly the powerhouses that other splats are, and their power source is a bit difficult to come by given it doesn't come from people. Honestly, I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T21:42:41-07:00","id":953663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=953622#post953622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> and Milo V3: Or we could not make the game angstier and thus remove one of it's selling points?</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who is so immensely anti &quot;make geist angsty&quot;, I find you saying that to me abit amusing :P<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't see &quot;this forest burned down&quot; or &quot;one of my possessions is broken&quot; as more angsty than &quot;because you fucked up, an innocent person has been killed&quot;, but whatever, YMMV. I was mainly just saying that death caused by you dying could apply to objects and places not just people IF it was tied to your touchstones (but I personally think touchstones should be stuff that reminds your geist of life rather than deathly things anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 08-19-2016, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T06:40:51-07:00","id":953799,"title":"","content":"I believe there needs to be a mechanic for the Geist to take control of the body. The Geist walked into the Bargain holding all the chips, and it makes no sense that afterwards they can just be ignored and defied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T06:56:24-07:00","id":953809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=953799#post953799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe there needs to be a mechanic for the Geist to take control of the body. The Geist walked into the Bargain holding all the chips, and it makes no sense that afterwards they can just be ignored and defied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at will, certainly, but I definitely think that there should be something like this. Perhaps if the Sin-Eater defies the geist (and risks Synergy in the process), the geist can try to posses them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T07:07:32-07:00","id":953813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=953622#post953622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lack of supernatural angst is a feature, not a bug. Don't fuck with it, that's the appeal. &quot;You made a deal. The person making the deal is so desperate that the deal is stacked heavily in your favor. You don't die and you get awesome powers. In exchange, your head guest would like it if you occasionally do things for it, and you're totally allowed to tell it to shut up and think of something else if you don't want to do what it asked you to do.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> and Milo V3: Or we could not make the game angstier and thus remove one of it's selling points?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps we read different version, but I've never seen Sin-Eaters as having been about &quot;lacking supernatural angst&quot;. It's there, it just as isn't in your face as other splats have. Sin-Eaters consider themselves to have made a good bargain, not gotten a freebie. The &quot;human gets all the benefits, no downsides&quot; is what makes no sense.<br /> <br /> As for losing Touchstones, that only happen if you screw up and die. The energy to bring you back has to come from <i>somewhere</i>. It's not like you've got god-like Sugar/Sekhem-Daddies like mummies do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=953653#post953653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a trade-off, while they're very hard to kill, <b>they're not exactly the powerhouses that other splats are</b>,</div> </div> </div> </div>Boneyard.<br /> <hr /><br /> Regarding Geist influence and control, what about things like the Tainted Condition from Requiem's influence on a die roll? Annoy your Geist, and it has a pool of Dice Modifiers it can spend to make life miserable/get you back on track.<br /> <br /> Although, I think much of what a Geist gets out of the Bargain is a chance to cheat death and &quot;live&quot; again through their Sin-Eater proxy. They are living the high life compared to the other dismal shades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-19-2016, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T07:44:23-07:00","id":953835,"title":"","content":"When I ran Geist, I ported over and hacked at the Possession rules from Inferno. I dont have my notes handy, but I believe I used something along these lines:<br /> <br /> Geist has a Willpower track identical to the Bound, and can spend a point to attempt a take over. The Bound can spend willpower to outright end the attempt. They both roll Resolve and composure. Winner takes control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T12:22:22-07:00","id":953950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=953663#post953663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who is so immensely anti &quot;make geist angsty&quot;, I find you saying that to me abit amusing :P<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't see &quot;this forest burned down&quot; or &quot;one of my possessions is broken&quot; as more angsty than &quot;because you fucked up, an innocent person has been killed&quot;, but whatever, YMMV. I was mainly just saying that death caused by you dying could apply to objects and places not just people IF it was tied to your touchstones (but I personally think touchstones should be stuff that reminds your geist of life rather than deathly things anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>Making the death or destruction caused by a Resurrection person gives them legitimate reason to angst... More so than if the death is random, at least. &quot;Random innocent died because you fucked up and got killed&quot; sounds about the right level of angst for this game to me.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=953799#post953799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe there needs to be a mechanic for the Geist to take control of the body. The Geist walked into the Bargain holding all the chips, and it makes no sense that afterwards they can just be ignored and defied.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> The Geist has some good chips, but the mortal has the two chips of the most value.<br /> <br /> The human can live, and thats the thing the Geist wants more than anything else.<br /> <br /> And the human can refuse the deal, and the geist has to leave.<br /> <br /> So in order to get what they really actually want, the Geist makes a bargain that the human isn't likely to refuse.<br /> <br /> Besides, the Geist being able to posses the host when the host isn't at Synergy Zero, that's a major inherent draw back. It makes it suck to be a Sin-Eater. Geists entire point is that it doesn't not suck to be a Sin-Eater.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=953813#post953813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps we read different version, but I've never seen Sin-Eaters as having been about &quot;lacking supernatural angst&quot;. It's there, it just as isn't in your face as other splats have. Sin-Eaters consider themselves to have made a good bargain, not gotten a freebie. The &quot;human gets all the benefits, no downsides&quot; is what makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernatural Angst is Angst about being a supernatural creature. Dem Bone's host has it, and that one week willed Sin-Eater whose geist bullies him into doing what it wants, probably has supernatural angst.<br /> <br /> Any of the wretched who are still conscious? They've got supernatural angst.<br /> <br /> A Sin-Eater who lives in a big city with a lot of murders and a lot of death, and who doesn't know the ceremonies to keep ghosts from bugging him at home, he might have a little angst until he learns the ceremony and picks up the skills to cope with occasionally stumbling across a place where somebody was murdered, but compared to the angst that a Vampire or a Werewolf or Promeathean might feel, that's a much easier thing to cope with.<br /> <br /> The Sin-Eater who keeps dying and getting innocent people killed? He's got legitimate reason to angst<br /> <br /> The vast majority of Sin-Eaters, however,do not have much legitimate reason to angst. Any average sin-eater who says &quot;Oh wow is me, I'm not dead and I have awesome powers, or why did I agree to this bargain that was overwhelmingly stacked in my favor&quot; is a sin-eater whose going to have the others wondering if he's crazy.<br /> <br /> There are already games about how much it sucks to be X-Supernatural creature. Leave Geist to be about accepting that death happens but that life is worth celebrating.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <hr />Although, I think much of what a Geist gets out of the Bargain is a chance to cheat death and &quot;live&quot; again through their Sin-Eater proxy. They are living the high life compared to the other dismal shades. </div> </div> </div>And they're willing to cut a deal that is horribly stacked against them to get it.<br /> <br /> What they want is to feel alive again, and they can only do that if the human agrees to the deal. So the deal is as sweet as it can be &quot;Hey, Mr... You're dying. I can fix that, but you've got to let me tag along with you... Oh, I'll even give you some sweet super powers... Yeah, and you just have to go out and live... Maybe watch stuff burn every so often... Some ghosts might want you to help them, but there are ways to get out of that if you really don't want to, and there are benefits to helping them pass on. So, do we have a deal?&quot;<br /> <br /> Take the core book, the Burning Woman's host is more than willing to watch stuff burn, but as soon as BW asks her to pour gasoline on people and light them up, BW gets told to shut the fuck up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 08-19-2016, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T12:38:03-07:00","id":953961,"title":"","content":"And thus far, it's the same. A switch to Touchstone instead of Random Person makes it more personal (and logical), but seriously, just don't die like a chump. Other splats don't get off nearly as easy. Geist <i>influence</i>, as opposed to outright control, lets the Geist make it's feelings felt and encourage co-operation, but you can still tell them to F' off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T13:35:10-07:00","id":954001,"title":"","content":"This is where we disagree. I don't see the Bargain stacked against the Geist. It is the reason the dead human gets to live again, it controls access to manifestations, and if the Human says no, the Geist has nothing but time. The Human has a meatsuit, and a strong desire to not die. The Geist is an entity of such power, that it has pulled itself free of the Underworld, and it defies definitions, being both a soul and a spirit. Possessing the meatsuit it shares with a mere human soul should /very/ much be a part daily life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T16:23:56-07:00","id":954090,"title":"","content":"I don't like the idea of geists possessing their bound, at least not until they are one of the wretched. But I do think the geists should get a greater amount of benefit from the bargain than they do right now, and that the level of manipulation they have over their bound should be better represented mechanically.<br /> <br /> I would suggest that geists get three aspirations themselves, which serve as the only way to increase your keys, manifestations and synergy as those elements are actually the geist doing the power and since synergy should require the bound and geist working together as a team. Also, when a bound &quot;Actively&quot; goes against one of their geists aspirations, it is a breaking point (likely with a modifier based on whether it's a short term or long term aspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T01:25:03-07:00","id":954270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=954001#post954001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is where we disagree. I don't see the Bargain stacked against the Geist. It is the reason the dead human gets to live again, it controls access to manifestations, and if the Human says no, the Geist has nothing but time. The Human has a meatsuit, and a strong desire to not die. The Geist is an entity of such power, that it has pulled itself free of the Underworld, and it defies definitions, being both a soul and a spirit. Possessing the meatsuit it shares with a mere human soul should /very/ much be a part daily life.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the human is just a meat suit that the Geist can posses at will, then Geist goes from the game that's the most upbeat with almost no supernatural angst as it's selling point to &quot;being a Sin-Eater sucks worse than being a promeathean.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, caore book--The bond between Geist and Sin-Eater is explicitly symbiosis, not possession. Giving the geists the power to posses the mortal goes against the definition of a sin-eater.<br /> <br /> Never mind the idea that maybe, just maybe, the reason Geists make the Bargain is because they can't claim or posses mortals like ghosts or spirits can? If they could posses, why go to the trouble of making the bargain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:46:44-07:00","id":954449,"title":"","content":"Gonna jump in and say I'm another who is fine with the idea of Synergy representing the level of patience a Geist has with their Sin-Eater. If it's such a big thing to represent a Geist's patience wavering and improving to wanna say 'f it' and get in the meat saddle, then Synergy could be made to be more like Werewolf's 2e Harmony track or Changeling 2e's Clarity where it's more fluid. However as a Geist player I feel enough dread comes from the worry of messing up and draining Synergy (as explicitly upon death and rebirth the max drops each time along with the dot drop) leaving my Sin-Eater as a Wretched.<br /> <br /> As mentioned above, the Bargain is more a level of symbiosis and I always feel the Geist is pretty chill just being able to experience life vicariously through their new Bound. Synergy dips when that Bound does something they don't like and you could say a Geist is just playing the waiting game, slowly getting more influence each time the Bound dies and collects death energy until they get Wretched. I feel the Geist knows what it's doing and it's fine sitting back until they get their turn in the driver's seat. Let's be real, it's kinda inevitable, as everything dies...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T12:06:38-07:00","id":954532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=954449#post954449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's be real, it's kinda inevitable, as everything dies...</div> </div> </div> </div>Geist can't bring you back from death by old age, so no, becoming a Wretched is not inevitable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T15:11:03-07:00","id":954643,"title":"","content":"Why does the body's original owner have total control? The two are now existing as a singular soul, the body belongs to them both. Why does the Geist immediately lose agency, and become dismissable on a whim? The game is about &quot;Second Chances&quot;, why does the Geist not get theirs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T15:37:09-07:00","id":954658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=954643#post954643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does the body's original owner have total control? The two are now existing as a singular soul, the body belongs to them both. Why does the Geist immediately lose agency, and become dismissable on a whim? The game is about &quot;Second Chances&quot;, why does the Geist not get theirs?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I don't think geists should possess their bound until they are wretched&quot; != &quot;Bodies original owner should have total control&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T22:09:30-07:00","id":954817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=954643#post954643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does the body's original owner have total control? The two are now existing as a singular soul, the body belongs to them both. Why does the Geist immediately lose agency, and become dismissable on a whim? The game is about &quot;Second Chances&quot;, why does the Geist not get theirs?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Geist gives up most of their agency in exchange for being able to feel alive again.<br /> <br /> The Geists second chance is being able to live vicariously through the host.<br /> <br /> The body's original owner almost always has full control because they were the agent who decided that the bond happened--the geist can't bond unless the host agrees. The host has most of the agency even before the bond is formed.<br /> <br /> The Sin-Eater might have to do somethings for the Geist, but telling it &quot;No, I will not set innocent people on fire, you have to be satisfied with this bonfire. is not the same as dismissing it on a whim.<br /> <br /> The geist being able to posses the Host at will goes against the theme of the game and a against the nature of the bond. Seriously, stop trying to make it suck to be a Sin-Eater. The fact that being a Sin-Eater doen'st suck is one of the game's selling points, one of the things that makes it distinct from the rest of the CroD and from Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T11:15:55-07:00","id":955029,"title":"","content":"You see suck, I see interesting. The interplay between Geist and Bound is laughable as written. Outright possession may be too much, but the Geist, as written, has no teeth. Why call it Synergy when the Bound has total, absolute control, until 0? <br /> <br /> The Splat can be positive in tone while also having downsides. Its a game about ghosts, possession, death and consequences. Having a downside does not mean there is suck. Conflict is required for a good story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T11:32:39-07:00","id":955040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=955029#post955029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You see suck, I see interesting. The interplay between Geist and Bound is laughable as written. Outright possession may be too much, but the Geist, as written, has no teeth. Why call it Synergy when the Bound has total, absolute control, until 0? <br /> <br /> The Splat can be positive in tone while also having downsides. Its a game about ghosts, possession, death and consequences. Having a downside does not mean there is suck. Conflict is required for a good story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps a geist has a kind of 1- or 2-dot Influence over the host? Spending Plasm (or some other kind of rare resource) in order to use it? That way, a geist could directly influence its host without needing to possess it fully. It could even be that the geist uses the Influence to help the host, waking them up if they're attacked, purging alcohol or poisons etc. Just an idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:29:32-07:00","id":955081,"title":"","content":"Well you can say the Bound are a type of Claimed (they kind of are, in a way...). Yes, I know the Bound don't have Essence (Ban and Bane also only come in through Krewe formation also), I'm not being completely literal by stating that, just that there are some similarities (Synergy represents the level of patience a Geist has with their Bound to me)... Anyway, you could look at the rules for Urging that a fresh Claimed tends to go through mid-fusion, though after that the pair are bonded into one soul.<br /> <br /> I'd play it that it's not that the Bound is in complete control, the Bound's personality you're rping is actually both the Geist and it's former mortal persona fused (this is going that your character starts the game as a Bound). Synergy thus represents the level of hold the mortal/Geist half has, though both the Geist and mortal together as the Bound have the singular personality you're roleplaying as the normal character. As Synergy dropped in 1e, a Bound could get disorders (same as Morality drops gave them) and this could be the rp element of the Geist's persona taking over. It wasn't so much of bouts of being Urged rather than a slow shift over to fully Other.<br /> <br /> Now how to represent this in 2e Geist, I'm not exactly sure. I like the idea of a somewhat more fluid and see-sawing Synergy though a Bound doesn't have their Geist possess them until Synergy 0, it's more like they're Claimed and Synergy is the level of shift between the fused's personalities as one side or another becomes more dominant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T19:57:34-07:00","id":955372,"title":"","content":"I'd blend Beast and Werewolf morality. High synergy creates a condition that improves ghostly manifestations, but saddles you with a Ban and Bane or makes it impossible to use the Virtue analogue to regain WP. Low Synergy improves physical manifestations, and a condition that is a persistent penalty equal to psyche because the Geist is trying to take over. Middle ground gives a bonus to ceremonies, but no penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:08:05-07:00","id":955659,"title":"","content":"I am very interested in what the changes to Ghosts in the CofD rulebook will mean to Geist. It's not a big change, but the book now mentions that not all ghosts are ectoplasmic VCR's reliving their old life, that there are a few ghosts that are self-aware and self-directed.<br /> <br /> My main hope is that instead of just one &quot;half-splat&quot; like most of the other CofD games have, that 2nd edition Geist would have - Living characters with some a singular death-related ability (mediumship, etc) and playable ghosts. I don't want Wraith redux but I don't think we need to avoid Ghost PC's just because Wraith: The Oblivion exists. Taken as a Ghoul-like supporting character, it might be cool.<br /> <br /> That's my hopes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9255-docsteve2020","name":"DocSteve2020","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:37:31-07:00","id":955683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DocSteve2020</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=955659#post955659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very interested in what the changes to Ghosts in the CofD rulebook will mean to Geist. It's not a big change, but the book now mentions that not all ghosts are ectoplasmic VCR's reliving their old life, that there are a few ghosts that are self-aware and self-directed.<br /> <br /> My main hope is that instead of just one &quot;half-splat&quot; like most of the other CofD games have, that 2nd edition Geist would have - Living characters with some a singular death-related ability (mediumship, etc) and playable ghosts. I don't want Wraith redux but I don't think we need to avoid Ghost PC's just because Wraith: The Oblivion exists. Taken as a Ghoul-like supporting character, it might be cool.<br /> <br /> That's my hopes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's my hope as well: a 2E Geist minor template similar to the Ghoul to a Vampire or the Wolf-Blooded to a Werewolf or a Sleepwalker/Proximi to a Mage or a Fae-Touched to a Changeling <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Maybe a Sin-Eater's supporting character is someone who died and returned without the aid of a Geist's bargain. Clinically dead, saw the Underworld or the Twilight, and was brought back medically, or mystically, leaving their soul with a touch of the Underworld's shades, but not a merging with a ghost or bargain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:33:13-07:00","id":955794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DocSteve2020</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=955659#post955659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very interested in what the changes to Ghosts in the CofD rulebook will mean to Geist. It's not a big change, but the book now mentions that not all ghosts are ectoplasmic VCR's reliving their old life, that there are a few ghosts that are self-aware and self-directed.<br /> <br /> My main hope is that instead of just one &quot;half-splat&quot; like most of the other CofD games have, that 2nd edition Geist would have - Living characters with some a singular death-related ability (mediumship, etc) and playable ghosts. I don't want Wraith redux but I don't think we need to avoid Ghost PC's just because Wraith: The Oblivion exists. Taken as a Ghoul-like supporting character, it might be cool.<br /> <br /> That's my hopes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got half formed notions of start a thread for a Ghost focused Chronicle take (rough name: Dead City: the Ghost Chronicles) that I've been meaning to post to the forums...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T03:15:34-07:00","id":956868,"title":"","content":"Regarding the influence of the geist, the Chrod editions expand what each line's virtue and vice analogues represent about a character. In the case of sineaters, vice could represent a principal drive of the geist, giving the sineater a cheap and easy way to built up willpower by doing what it wants - while the virtue is rooter in their former life, harder to fully pursue with the demands of their new existence, but more fulfilling.<br /> <br /> That would also illustrate the unusual nature of geist &quot;possession,&quot; in that following either their own or the geist's drives can fulfill a sineater's sense of self.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a different subject, some of the writing for keys and manifestations implies that the first level power of a given manifestation has to be activated before any higher level can be - so high level powers are two actions and two rolls. Assuming keys and manifestations are structured the same way, I'd like that to explicitly be the case, because it goes well with the idea of unlocking, and somewhat offsets the versatility of sineater powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T08:18:36-07:00","id":956980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=956868#post956868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the influence of the geist, the Chrod editions expand what each line's virtue and vice analogues represent about a character. In the case of sineaters, vice could represent a principal drive of the geist, giving the sineater a cheap and easy way to built up willpower by doing what it wants - while the virtue is rooter in their former life, harder to fully pursue with the demands of their new existence, but more fulfilling.<br /> <br /> That would also illustrate the unusual nature of geist &quot;possession,&quot; in that following either their own or the geist's drives can fulfill a sineater's sense of self.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=956868#post956868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a different subject, some of the writing for keys and manifestations implies that the first level power of a given manifestation has to be activated before any higher level can be - so high level powers are two actions and two rolls. Assuming keys and manifestations are structured the same way, I'd like that to explicitly be the case, because it goes well with the idea of unlocking, and somewhat offsets the versatility of sineater powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? I always thought it was pretty clear that the higher dot effects are upgrades to the base effect. You only &quot;unlock&quot; once, but the benefits you get varies depending on your skill level with the Manifestation and what Key you are using.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T08:44:13-07:00","id":957639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=956868#post956868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the influence of the geist, the Chrod editions expand what each line's virtue and vice analogues represent about a character. In the case of sineaters, vice could represent a principal drive of the geist, giving the sineater a cheap and easy way to built up willpower by doing what it wants - while the virtue is rooter in their former life, harder to fully pursue with the demands of their new existence, but more fulfilling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought this was a good way to handle it, but on top of that, I would also give Sin-Eater's a 4th Aspiration that is their Geist's Aspiration. Low Synergy should also cause penalties to some powers and actions too. All of these things would encourage you to do what your Geist wants without it stealing control from you.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T08:55:57-07:00","id":957646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=957639#post957639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought this was a good way to handle it, but on top of that, I would also give Sin-Eater's a 4th Aspiration that is their Geist's Aspiration. Low Synergy should also cause penalties to some powers and actions too. All of these things would encourage you to do what your Geist wants without it stealing control from you.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as it stands now, Synergy is used in some dice pools, so low Synergy has its own inherent drawback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T17:32:35-07:00","id":957944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=955029#post955029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You see suck, I see interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sucks to be a vampire.<br /> It sucks to be a werewolf.<br /> It kind of sucks to be a mage sometimes.<br /> Sometimes it sucks to be a hunter.<br /> Being a Promethean sucks so bad that the entire point of the game is &quot;stop being a promeathean&quot;<br /> It sucks to become a changeling and usually sucks to live as a changeling.<br /> It sort of sucks to be a Mummy, what with the amnesia and the basically always getting weaker and the being a slave.<br /> Demons have to live in constant hiding from an enemy that's literally everywhere, so yeah, it sucks to be them too.<br /> Beast: A lot of your relatives are assholes, and the people that are dedicated to wiping your kind out mostly go after folks like you who aren't hurting anyone since they're the easiest to find. Kinda sucks, doesn't it.<br /> You can tell that being a Deviant sucks just from how the game is described.<br /> <br /> Being a Sin-Eater has no innate downsides. If being a Sin-Eater sucks, it's because that particular Sin-Eater either screwed up and died, because he's got an unusually inhuman geist(not the default assumption), or because he's too week willed to stand up to his geist(and PCs are assumed to not be spineless)<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters are the only splat where it doesn't suck to be one and live as one on a day today basis. Let them keep that.<br /> <br /> I mean, the fact that they're the only one that it really doesn't suck to be makes them unique. Unique is more interesting that same as everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 08-25-2016, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T20:36:25-07:00","id":958031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=957944#post957944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sucks to be a vampire.<br /> It sucks to be a werewolf.<br /> It kind of sucks to be a mage sometimes.<br /> Sometimes it sucks to be a hunter.<br /> Being a Promethean sucks so bad that the entire point of the game is &quot;stop being a promeathean&quot;<br /> It sucks to become a changeling and usually sucks to live as a changeling.<br /> It sort of sucks to be a Mummy, what with the amnesia and the basically always getting weaker and the being a slave.<br /> Demons have to live in constant hiding from an enemy that's literally everywhere, so yeah, it sucks to be them too.<br /> Beast: A lot of your relatives are assholes, and the people that are dedicated to wiping your kind out mostly go after folks like you who aren't hurting anyone since they're the easiest to find. Kinda sucks, doesn't it.<br /> You can tell that being a Deviant sucks just from how the game is described.<br /> <br /> Being a Sin-Eater has no innate downsides. If being a Sin-Eater sucks, it's because that particular Sin-Eater either screwed up and died, because he's got an unusually inhuman geist(not the default assumption), or because he's too week willed to stand up to his geist(and PCs are assumed to not be spineless)<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters are the only splat where it doesn't suck to be one and live as one on a day today basis. Let them keep that.<br /> <br /> I mean, the fact that they're the only one that it really doesn't suck to be makes them unique. Unique is more interesting that same as everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, even with the proposed changes, being a Sin-Eater still wouldn't suck. Certainly not in comparison to every other splat.<br /> <br /> And, I believe it should be mentioned: &quot;the nail that sticks out gets hammered down.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T21:49:52-07:00","id":958053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=958031#post958031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, I believe it should be mentioned: &quot;the nail that sticks out gets hammered down.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>.... because unique themes are bad now?<br /> <br /> *Shrug* I think Geists should get more freedom, let them give Bound conditions so they can steer them towards stuff, but anything close to actual possession seems wrong for Geist unless they are possessing the bound's corpse between resurrections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T23:14:16-07:00","id":958078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=958031#post958031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, even with the proposed changes, being a Sin-Eater still wouldn't suck. Certainly not in comparison to every other splat.<br /> <br /> And, I believe it should be mentioned: &quot;the nail that sticks out gets hammered down.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is specifically in regards to the &quot;Geists should be able to posses the Sin-Eater whenever the hell they want&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> I mean seriously, most Geists are content to sit back and experience the simple pleasures and sensations of life secondhand through their host. For every geist who will try and bully you into doing what it wants, there are geists who get along with you or at the very least know that it's in their best interests for their host to stay happy and healthy. Bad geists are consistently depicted as being an NPC thing, not a player thing.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters are supposed to have little to no supernatural angst. That is a feature, not a bug. Making all geists assholes who can and will steal control of your body whenever it damn well feels like it ruins that.<br /> <br /> It also makes no fucking sense--If Geists could posses or claim... Then they wouldn't bother with making deals, they'd just grab whatever body was convenient and ride it until the host rejected it or burned out.<br /> <br /> You want the geist to have more influence? Go with what's been said, an extra aspiration or an extra vice or virtue equivalent that gives you a reward--some willpower or plasm or a positive condition for doing things your geist likes. Carrots, not sticks. sticks are downsides. downsides make it suck to be a splat, and it not sucking to be a sin-eater is kind of the point.<br /> <br /> You take that away, you've got to take away Promethean's built in happy ending, and Mummy's starting at ten and counting down, and Beast's crossover compatibility, and stuff that makes the other lines unique because they've all got at least one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T11:01:49-07:00","id":959905,"title":"","content":"I think there is more to what makes Giest unique then being one isn't hellish.<br /> <br /> I think both mages and sin eaters need some kind of weaknesses to balance them with other splats, like a certain substance creates an superneral magic dead zone, and a Sin Eater can be killed of you find its Geists remains or last grave if it has no remains left, and salt them with a particular kind of sea salt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T13:57:03-07:00","id":960007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=959905#post959905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think both mages and sin eaters need some kind of weaknesses to balance them with other splats, like a certain substance creates an superneral magic dead zone</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it is called &quot;sleepers&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T17:56:35-07:00","id":960132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=959905#post959905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is more to what makes Giest unique then being one isn't hellish.<br /> <br /> I think both mages and sin eaters need some kind of weaknesses to balance them with other splats, like a certain substance creates an superneral magic dead zone, and a Sin Eater can be killed of you find its Geists remains or last grave if it has no remains left, and salt them with a particular kind of sea salt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geists are either Sprits that atea ghost and became a psudo malgath, or ghosts that have lost all of their Anchors and claimed their manner of death a s a anchor, thus forsaking humanity, to have a chance to escape the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Possibly both depending on the geist.<br /> <br /> Regardless, either way there wouldn't be remains or a last grave to salt and burn.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't think Sin-Eater need a weakness beyond what they've already got. If they actually need one it shouldn't be &quot;doing this thing instantly kills them&quot; it should be &quot;this thing kind of inconveniences them and can be used as a weapon. Maybe certain powerful anti-ghost thingies can force their geist to go temporarily dormant, inhibiting a Sin-Eater's ability to use plasm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T11:19:23-07:00","id":960560,"title":"","content":"I missed the early part of this thread, so some or all of what I'm saying here may already be covered.<br /> <br /> I suspect that 2e will be redefining the origins of geists; first, put a stake in the heart of the &quot;geists are ghosts that ate spirits&quot; theory, because the 2e notion that ghosts and spirits exist in separate Twilights makes that idea nearly unworkable. If you <i>must</i> keep it, shift it from &quot;ghost who ate spirit&quot; to &quot;ghost who ate chthonian&quot;; but my suspicion is that 2e's geists will be Rank 3+ ghosts who are evolving toward an inhuman state of being, and who's part of the Bargain is to reconnect with humanity: from the geist's perspective, his bond-mate serves as a Touchstone. <br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind the player's geist having its own Aspiration; I wouldn't mind if the Archetypes get recast as a third Anchor alongside Virtue and Vice and representing the geist's motive in offering the bargain. I wouldn't even mind if the geist provides one or two Synergy Breaking Points that stem from the mortal host doing things that the geist vehemently opposes. But that's as coercive as I'd want to go. Sin-Eaters aren't the Possessed from <b>Inferno</b>; the relationship between geist and mortal is a lot more... mutually beneficial, and cooperative. Symbiotic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T11:55:47-07:00","id":960578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=960560#post960560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I missed the early part of this thread, so some or all of what I'm saying here may already be covered.<br /> <br /> I suspect that 2e will be redefining the origins of geists; first, put a stake in the heart of the &quot;geists are ghosts that ate spirits&quot; theory, because the 2e notion that ghosts and spirits exist in separate Twilights makes that idea nearly unworkable. If you <i>must</i> keep it, shift it from &quot;ghost who ate spirit&quot; to &quot;ghost who ate chthonian&quot;; but my suspicion is that 2e's geists will be Rank 3+ ghosts who are evolving toward an inhuman state of being, and who's part of the Bargain is to reconnect with humanity: from the geist's perspective, his bond-mate serves as a Touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geists are ghosts who drink from a River in the underworld. Spoiled by Travis in another thread (although he said mage already spoiled it): <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=960561#post960561\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...561#post960561</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T15:46:42-07:00","id":960716,"title":"","content":"I know it's a longshot- but is there any chance we'll see something in the style of Lucid Dead Numen from Mummy in the new edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T19:19:03-07:00","id":960802,"title":"","content":"A long shot? I'd say it's <i>likely</i>: according to the new Ephemeral Entity rules, all rank 2+ ghosts are lucid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T15:57:16-07:00","id":961942,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see more done with the boundary of life and death. What is agency; astral projection, akasha, etc. With the concept of ghosts, I'd like to see a focus on the duality of Fetters vs Liberty. We are bound by our fetters, and that's not a bad thing. Fetters keep us attached to reality. Sensation is a fetter, Sanity is a fetter, as are people, places and beliefs. But we are not honest about what binds us. We seek unlimited freedom, but are we honest about what makes us free.<br /> <br /> Could I pick up the fetters of a young girl ghost, taking her place in the world until what still binds her to world is freed?<br /> Can the powers that I gain be expressed in the terms of freedom - free to walk through walls, free to ignore the need to breath/eat, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1411-wingnut2292","name":"wingnut2292","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1411_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T22:06:29-07:00","id":962087,"title":"","content":"I'd like the game to make more elaboration on the Twilight network. As it is, the disparate elements about it just do not make sense to me, and...well, I cannot make heads or tails of how it is supposed to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T07:07:46-07:00","id":962245,"title":"","content":"I have been using a few darknet sites as a local Twilight Network that the Krewes use in our area. Also, those that don't know of it use more symbolic approaches. Obituaries, cemeteries, etc. I've always viewed it as just a communication network that the krewes use to inform each other of things locally and abroad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T07:20:12-07:00","id":962259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EldritchMinister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=962245#post962245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been using a few darknet sites as a local Twilight Network that the Krewes use in our area. Also, those that don't know of it use more symbolic approaches. Obituaries, cemeteries, etc. I've always viewed it as just a communication network that the krewes use to inform each other of things locally and abroad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as the guy who wrote the Twilight Network section in 1e, yeah, that was all it was ever really meant to be. There was a period, I think, where the old nWoD was <i>really</i> into old 1930s hobo codes, and the Twilight Network was sort of an outgrowth of that. 2nd Edition will talk a little bit about ways Sin-Eaters might leave secret signs or messages for her, but don't expect it to be a major element with a Fancy Proper Noun. Like most things in Sin-Eater culture, it's ad hoc, invented whole cloth, forgotten, rediscovered, forgotten again, and independently reinvented later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T08:06:03-07:00","id":962291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=953622#post953622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The lack of supernatural angst is a feature, not a bug. Don't fuck with it, that's the appeal. &quot;You made a deal. The person making the deal is so desperate that the deal is stacked heavily in your favor. You don't die and you get awesome powers. In exchange, your head guest would like it if you occasionally do things for it, and you're totally allowed to tell it to shut up and think of something else if you don't want to do what it asked you to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never looked at the Bargain as inherently stacked heavily in the favor of the Sin-Eater. I've always thought that it should vary from character to character. Sure, one gets the advantage of a Geist who is content to tag along and live vicariously, but I see that as the exception rather than the rule. Others want more. I see it as less, &quot;Please, Mr. Dying Mortal, don't die on me yet. I'll give you another chance at life, and super powers, just please, let me tag along with you. Please, accept my offer. Pretty please?&quot; I've always seen it more as &quot;Ah, here you are, Mr. Dying Mortal, about to shuffle off this mortal coil. I hope you did everything you needed to in life... Oh, you're not ready yet? You still have things you'd like to do? Unfinished business among the living, perhaps? Well, that's just fine. You see, I can give you the chance to take care of that. I can give you another chance. In exchange, you do something for me. I scratch your back, you scratch mine. Now, here are my terms. Take it or leave it.&quot; I've always looked at it as the Geist holding most of the chips in the Bargain, and that it is the lucky Sin-Eaters that get ones that only want to ride around in the mortal world for awhile. I think that the Bargain should have consequences beyond just a second chance for the Sin-Eater. I don't think that a Sin-Eater should get to come back to life, hear the Geist say, &quot;Okay, now it's your turn to hold up your end of our Bargain,&quot; and have the Sin-Eater respond with, &quot;Fuck off, I already got mine, so I don't need to hold up my end, and there's not a thing you can do about it,&quot; to which the Geist responds, &quot;Crap, you're right. Umm... Please...&quot; I never really ran it that way. For instance, one of my characters was a lazy stoner who made an agreement with a Geist called Idle Hands who had been a mass murderer in life. In exchange for being allowed to live again, he agreed to the Geist's Bargain, which involved killing one person a month. After he was back, he blew off the Bargain, and went back to doing what he had been doing. At the end of the first month, Idle Hands took control, and forced his end of the Bargain. After that, the Sin-Eater realized that his Bargain was actually binding, and so now, the world's laziest man has become a Reaper, desperately searching for someone who deserves it to remove from the world before his Geist takes matters into its own hands and picks someone at random. If the Bargain has no teeth, then that concept would be totally invalid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T11:10:13-07:00","id":962380,"title":"","content":"Travis, very cool. That is definitely one thing that has always appealed to me with Geist and the Bound as a whole. The fact that we can really perceive it in a way that appeals to us and our players and go from there. Basically, a skeleton of how it works and we get to add the meat. I'm definitely looking forward to the 2nd edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T09:04:57-07:00","id":962845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=962291#post962291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've never looked at the Bargain as inherently stacked heavily in the favor of the Sin-Eater. I've always thought that it should vary from character to character. Sure, one gets the advantage of a Geist who is content to tag along and live vicariously, but I see that as the exception rather than the rule. Others want more. I see it as less, &quot;Please, Mr. Dying Mortal, don't die on me yet. I'll give you another chance at life, and super powers, just please, let me tag along with you. Please, accept my offer. Pretty please?&quot; I've always seen it more as &quot;Ah, here you are, Mr. Dying Mortal, about to shuffle off this mortal coil. I hope you did everything you needed to in life... Oh, you're not ready yet? You still have things you'd like to do? Unfinished business among the living, perhaps? Well, that's just fine. You see, I can give you the chance to take care of that. I can give you another chance. In exchange, you do something for me. I scratch your back, you scratch mine. Now, here are my terms. Take it or leave it.&quot; I've always looked at it as the Geist holding most of the chips in the Bargain, and that it is the lucky Sin-Eaters that get ones that only want to ride around in the mortal world for awhile. I think that the Bargain should have consequences beyond just a second chance for the Sin-Eater. I don't think that a Sin-Eater should get to come back to life, hear the Geist say, &quot;Okay, now it's your turn to hold up your end of our Bargain,&quot; and have the Sin-Eater respond with, &quot;Fuck off, I already got mine, so I don't need to hold up my end, and there's not a thing you can do about it,&quot; to which the Geist responds, &quot;Crap, you're right. Umm... Please...&quot; I never really ran it that way. For instance, one of my characters was a lazy stoner who made an agreement with a Geist called Idle Hands who had been a mass murderer in life. In exchange for being allowed to live again, he agreed to the Geist's Bargain, which involved killing one person a month. After he was back, he blew off the Bargain, and went back to doing what he had been doing. At the end of the first month, Idle Hands took control, and forced his end of the Bargain. After that, the Sin-Eater realized that his Bargain was actually binding, and so now, the world's laziest man has become a Reaper, desperately searching for someone who deserves it to remove from the world before his Geist takes matters into its own hands and picks someone at random. If the Bargain has no teeth, then that concept would be totally invalid.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading makes it very clear that Geists that are happy to just sit around are the rule, rather than the exception.<br /> <br /> That fits with the theme--the world is a dark and scary place, but life is worth living, you're alive, and that's worth celebrating.<br /> <br /> The Bargain flat out does not happen if the mortal doen'st agree. this is explicit. The mortal is the one who decided that the Bargain happens.<br /> <br /> The Geist can not force the host to do anything. <i>Completely</i> refusing to bend can<u> lower your synergy,</u> but that's but it. The geist can yell and scream and cuss, but it <i>can not</i> posses you, can not take control of your body from you, can not force you to do shit, unless you're one of the Wretched. This is explicit. The Bargain is explicitly not possession. The closet thing to this is a single NPC who was completely spineless and let his giest bully him into doing what it wants.<br /> <br /> Idle Hands, going by the strict rules, flat out can not take control of the Lazy Stoner by the strict rules of the game and by the themes of the game. You played the game as much darker than it's meant to be. Which is fine, it's your game you can do what you want with it, but that is not the default and should not be the default. The default should be the one game with no supernatural angsy, as this is the selling point.<br /> <br /> The game makes it clear that most geists, most of all, want to be alive again.<br /> <br /> The game mentions one Sin-Eater keeping a serial killing geist locked up tight in her soul, and the host of the Burning Woman is explicitly stated to tell her geist to shut the fuck up whenever her geist tells her to pour gasoline over a human being and set them on fire. If the geists could force their hosts to do hat the want, then neither of these would be possible.<br /> <br /> All of this together makes it abundantly clear that the mortal holds all of the chips before and during the Bargain.<br /> <br /> You want to play a Sin-Eater who gets bullied into doing what it's geist wants? Fine, there's sup[port for that in the rules, but that is not the default assumption of the game, and your characters experience sucks far worse than the default simply because he doen'st realize that he has most of the power in the relationship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 09-03-2016, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T04:02:06-07:00","id":963152,"title":"","content":"In the movies, it always seems to create a lot of angst for mortals that can see ghosts. I guess if you can turn it off that would lessen, but if ghosts can recognize sin-eaters then I imagine they can come up with a way to get their attention anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":".  deleted because it was the wrong thread then reclaimed because this one hadn't moved too far 09-04-2016, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T08:24:30-07:00","id":963231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=962845#post962845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My reading makes it very clear that Geists that are happy to just sit around are the rule, rather than the exception.<br /> <br /> That fits with the theme--the world is a dark and scary place, but life is worth living, you're alive, and that's worth celebrating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, life is worth living. So much that it is worth chaining yourself to a horrific embodiment of death just for another sweet taste of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=962845#post962845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bargain flat out does not happen if the mortal doen'st agree. this is explicit. The mortal is the one who decided that the Bargain happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bargain also doesn't happen if the geist does not offer it. I can walk into a car dealership, sign the offered loan application, and drive away in a new car (well, some people could, at any rate), but payments still need to be made on the loan. If that scenario worked the way the Bargain is being interpreted here, then I would be able to do that, the car would be mine, and the worst that the dealership could do if I decided not to pay would be to make angry phone calls at all hours of the night. That would mean that, not only does the Bargain have fewer negative consequences than any other supernatural agreement, it also has fewer negative consequences than even ordinary mortal agreements. It makes the Bargain more akin to winning the lottery than entering into an agreement with a supposedly helpful entity. That doesn't really seem fitting in the horror genre to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=962845#post962845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Geist can not force the host to do anything. <i>Completely</i> refusing to bend can<u> lower your synergy,</u> but that's but it. The geist can yell and scream and cuss, but it <i>can not</i> posses you, can not take control of your body from you, can not force you to do shit, unless you're one of the Wretched. This is explicit. The Bargain is explicitly not possession. The closet thing to this is a single NPC who was completely spineless and let his giest bully him into doing what it wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Bargain should be binding to both sides of it, not just one. If lower Synergy is going to be the only downside to violating the Bargain, then lower Synergy should be a bit more problematic than just a penalty to doing Ceremonies or other ghost-related things and navigating the Underworld. If a Sin-Eater is just wanting to go about his or her everyday life as they had been before, then low Synergy is largely meaningless, at least until something goes awry and they end up dead again. As an aside, I think that Synergy should remain high if the Sin-Eater is acting in accordance with the geist's wishes, even if the geist desires horrific things. A geist of torture that makes the Bargain with a torturer shouldn't find Synergy plummeting because the two of them go on a torture spree. High Synergy with a horrific geist should be terrifying to everyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=962845#post962845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idle Hands, going by the strict rules, flat out can not take control of the Lazy Stoner by the strict rules of the game and by the themes of the game. You played the game as much darker than it's meant to be. Which is fine, it's your game you can do what you want with it, but that is not the default and should not be the default. The default should be the one game with no supernatural angsy, as this is the selling point.</div> </div> </div> </div>This last point is where we disagree. Sure, the rules of the game make it so that Idle Hands would have little to do besides drive the Bound insane, but I disagree that that should be the way of it, and I disagree that the selling point of Geist is that there is no supernatural angst. Yes, it has an atmosphere of celebrating life in the face of death, and that is awesome. That's not the same thing as there being a lack of downsides to one's condition. If anything, it should be embracing the good and the bad of life, accepting it all together and saying that it's worth it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=962845#post962845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game makes it clear that most geists, most of all, want to be alive again.<br /> <br /> The game mentions one Sin-Eater keeping a serial killing geist locked up tight in her soul, and the host of the Burning Woman is explicitly stated to tell her geist to shut the fuck up whenever her geist tells her to pour gasoline over a human being and set them on fire. If the geists could force their hosts to do hat the want, then neither of these would be possible.<br /> <br /> All of this together makes it abundantly clear that the mortal holds all of the chips before and during the Bargain.<br /> <br /> You want to play a Sin-Eater who gets bullied into doing what it's geist wants? Fine, there's sup[port for that in the rules, but that is not the default assumption of the game, and your characters experience sucks far worse than the default simply because he doen'st realize that he has most of the power in the relationship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that character's experience sucked worse than a lot of others. That was kind of the point to the character. But the Bargain should be binding regardless of the terms. A geist that bargained for its Sin-Eater to sample a new food or experience a new pleasure when the opportunity arises should have every expectation of having the Bargain honored. As a general rule, the player gets to decide what the terms of the Bargain would have been, so it would be up to the player how much friction there is between the geist and the Sin-Eater. I think that that is an area that should be explored more, and part of that is making it so that the Bargain is binding. I'm not saying that the Sin-Eater shouldn't be able to violate the Bargain, but that there should be consequences to doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T16:37:09-07:00","id":963442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Bargain also doesn't happen if the geist does not offer it. I can walk into a car dealership, sign the offered loan application, and drive away in a new car (well, some people could, at any rate), but payments still need to be made on the loan. </div> </div> </div>You've got the wrong idea about it.<br /> <br /> The Bargain is you buying the car outright--no loan, no downpayment. Anything the geist asks you to do after the fact is &quot;the friend who sold you a car is asking you for a favor. Saying no might harm your friendship, but are you really willing to do it?&quot;<br /> <br /> The bargain is&quot;you get to live again and get super powers, but ghosts might bother you, I get to tag along and live vicariously through you, and I might ask you to do things.&quot; The geist can lie, of course, but the Geist explicitly has no abillity to posses you, and no abillity to force you to do anything. It is giving you a car and hoping that you'll drive it where it wants to go.<br /> <br /> And I think that it should stay that way. Literally every gameline has people angsting baout being a supernatural being. Let the Sin-Eaters stay the one splat where the majority of them are perfectly happy to have made the Bargain.<br /> <br /> Reading the entire book, that in consistently how the Bargain is depicted. The only time that it's depicted as a bad thing<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not saying that the Sin-Eater shouldn't be able to violate the Bargain, but that there should be consequences to doing so. </div> </div> </div>There are. It's called your geist doens't like you very much, so your synergy is low and it might leave you to perma-die if you screw up and get killed.<br /> <br /> Ain't nothing wrong with the Geist having things it'd like you to do. An extra vice or virtue or aspiration. The problem comes when you decide to violate one of the tenants of the game(this is the one splat where the majority of people like being one and don't think it sucks) and the nature of the Bargain(explicitly symbiosis, not possession) to give the gesit the abillty to take control of the Sin-eater and force their host to do morally reprehensible things. That takes the game from &quot;mostly happily formor dead people living life to the fullest, stopping hauntings, and putting ghosts to rest&quot; to &quot;the Promeathean's have it easier becuase at least they have a happy ending.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, if you want the geist to have some influence on the Sin-Eater, you want the Sin-Eater to have a reason to do what the geist wants, do it within the framework of the themes of the game.<br /> <br /> Carrots, not sticks. Doing things your geist likes, like clensing an abandoned prison husnted by executed murders by burning it to the ground, or going out of your way to stop and take pictures of the forest fire you drove by in the case of the Burning Woman, that should give you plasm or will power or make buying up your synergy easier. Rewards.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the sin-eater who refuses to do anything his geist asks, even if it's as simple as bathing more often, he's punished by having less willpower and plasm and having lower synergy than a Sin-Eater who is willing to negociate a deal with his Geist and do things that the geist likes as long as they're not too out there. He's punished by having a bad relationship with his geist with all of atendant draw backs that comes with it, not by his Geist possessing him and making him do what it wants.<br /> <br /> Unless he's hit Synergy Zero, but that's an exception, not the rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T09:33:28-07:00","id":964335,"title":"","content":"I don't think all or even most Sin Eaters love being what they are, they have creepy, crazy ghost in their head and they attract creepy ghosts like flies to shit. They happy about the upsides, not being dead, a second or more chance at life, and for getting cool powers, but there is plenty of reasons for Sin Eaters to be angsty, that have an insane ghost in they're head, 24/7.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:47:15-07:00","id":964440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=963442#post963442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've got the wrong idea about it.<br /> <br /> The Bargain is you buying the car outright--no loan, no downpayment. Anything the geist asks you to do after the fact is &quot;the friend who sold you a car is asking you for a favor. Saying no might harm your friendship, but are you really willing to do it?&quot;<br /> <br /> The bargain is&quot;you get to live again and get super powers, but ghosts might bother you, I get to tag along and live vicariously through you, and I might ask you to do things.&quot; The geist can lie, of course, but the Geist explicitly has no abillity to posses you, and no abillity to force you to do anything. It is giving you a car and hoping that you'll drive it where it wants to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your analogy, so we'll go with that one. Obviously, you can't get rid of your friend, so it's in the car with you, whether you like it or not. Yes, you're in the driver seat, and you get to choose the destination, but your friend could threaten you. It could pull a gun, or jerk the wheel, or cover your eyes. Your friend isn't hogtied in the backseat, with the gag having slipped out of its mouth, whining for you to stop for a cheeseburger on the way. It is right there with you, and its distractions should be dangerous, not merely annoying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=963442#post963442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I think that it should stay that way. Literally every gameline has people angsting baout being a supernatural being. Let the Sin-Eaters stay the one splat where the majority of them are perfectly happy to have made the Bargain.<br /> <br /> Reading the entire book, that in consistently how the Bargain is depicted. The only time that it's depicted as a bad thing<br /> <br /> There are. It's called your geist doens't like you very much, so your synergy is low and it might leave you to perma-die if you screw up and get killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that Sin-Eaters shouldn't like being what they are, or at least like having another shot at life. There should be upsides and downsides, even if the average Sin-Eater feels that the former outweigh the latter. There are plenty of things for a Sin-Eater to like. It shouldn't require a secret rite that can only be performed once a century when the moon is in the eighth house of Aquarius in order to find a downside. Yes, the characters of every other splat have problems. That should be expected. Everything in the Chronicles of Darkness comes with a price. Mortals are everyone's food and/or playthings. Hunters get the mortal package, plus get a few extra tools for the job in exchange for needing to lead a double life and be in a position where monsters are more likely to take notice of them. Vampires trade their days for an eternity of nights. Werewolves need to hunt and avoid silver, but are awakened to a world of sensations that others can't imagine. Mages can do just about anything, but cause trouble just using their magic. Changelings and demons choose how they'll live their lives, but they still need to watch their backs at all times. Mummies get eternity and great power, at the cost of memory and a tendency to oversleep. Beasts must feed. Prometheans are Prometheans. Each of them have some things that are awesome, and some things that suck. They're horror games. So is Geist. That's why it seems odd to me that they would be the one supernatural creature that completely lacks in downsides. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=963442#post963442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ain't nothing wrong with the Geist having things it'd like you to do. An extra vice or virtue or aspiration. The problem comes when you decide to violate one of the tenants of the game(this is the one splat where the majority of people like being one and don't think it sucks) and the nature of the Bargain(explicitly symbiosis, not possession) to give the gesit the abillty to take control of the Sin-eater and force their host to do morally reprehensible things. That takes the game from &quot;mostly happily formor dead people living life to the fullest, stopping hauntings, and putting ghosts to rest&quot; to &quot;the Promeathean's have it easier becuase at least they have a happy ending.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree that the Sin-Eaters needing to uphold their end of the Bargain would put them in a position that was worse off than the Promethean condition. First, Prometheans don't necessarily get a happy ending in the first place. They trade the Promethean package for the mortal one, and there's no guarantee that they'll be happy with the results once they have them. One of my major villains for one chronicle was a Promethean that had finally managed to achieve the gift of humanity, and wished that he'd kept the receipt. That said, it seems that the default assumption of Geist is that the player decides on the terms of the Bargain. A player who wishes for a geist that just wants their character to go out and have a good time is totally achievable within that framework. If most geists really just wish to vicariously experience life again like you said previously, then that would even be a more common Bargain. Even if the geist could possess the host for violating the terms of the Bargain, it wouldn't be likely to come up for most Sin-Eaters if the average geist just wants you to go dancing or grab a milkshake once a week. Regardless of how many Sin-Eaters regretted their Bargains, the player characters would still on average be the ones that were content with it, unless the players wanted the friction between geist and Bound from the beginning. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=963442#post963442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if you want the geist to have some influence on the Sin-Eater, you want the Sin-Eater to have a reason to do what the geist wants, do it within the framework of the themes of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here, I think we can both agree with that statement. I simply disagree that it must all be good things in order for it to remain within theme. Personally, I think that if there's only one Sin-Eater in a thousand that even entertains second thoughts about the Bargain, having any number of Sin-Eater antagonists that have problems with their geists will begin to fray my suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=963442#post963442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carrots, not sticks. Doing things your geist likes, like clensing an abandoned prison husnted by executed murders by burning it to the ground, or going out of your way to stop and take pictures of the forest fire you drove by in the case of the Burning Woman, that should give you plasm or will power or make buying up your synergy easier. Rewards.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the sin-eater who refuses to do anything his geist asks, even if it's as simple as bathing more often, he's punished by having less willpower and plasm and having lower synergy than a Sin-Eater who is willing to negociate a deal with his Geist and do things that the geist likes as long as they're not too out there. He's punished by having a bad relationship with his geist with all of atendant draw backs that comes with it, not by his Geist possessing him and making him do what it wants.<br /> <br /> Unless he's hit Synergy Zero, but that's an exception, not the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here, we disagree once more. I think that there should be carrots and sticks, not just one or the other. Fortunately, the Condition system of the Chronicles of Darkness makes it easy to do that, simply by having a set of positive Conditions that you can gain for high Synergy and a set of negative ones for low Synergy. Make it a collection of Conditions to choose between, and then the people who want the geist to be able to take control could have something like a Geist-Ridden Condition that can hit at low Synergy, and those who want the geist to be forever in the passenger seat could take something like a Distracted Condition instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T16:31:33-07:00","id":964613,"title":"","content":"I think its a safe bet at the very least, having a Psyche over 5 will agian come with disadvabtages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T15:11:01-07:00","id":965289,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing: Geists do not posses their hosts. The bargain is<b> explicitly not posses</b>. This is stated, flat out, in the introduction. The closest thing to possesion is the host <i>reverse </i>possesing their geist,<br /> <br /> If the geist can posses you, the geist <i>will </i>posses you. You can't play a character like the example host of the burning woman or the woman who keeps a serial killer locked up in her soul, because the geist will just flat out posses you if you don't set your enemies on fire or go out and randomly kill people. And that sucks worse than Prometheans, because Prometheans at least have a way out of their &quot;the world itself literally hates you&quot; state.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, and I've said this before, but it makes <b>no sense </b>for the Geist to be able to posses it's host. If Geists had the power to posses mortals at all, then why would they even bother with the Bargain? They would just posses any convenient mortal and ride them until they broke down. The fact that they make the Bargain instead of posssing mortals tells me that they can't posses mortals.<br /> <br /> Finally, actually reading the book, the vast Majority of Sin-Eaters are not all angsty like other splats--It sucks to be a Vampire. It sucks to be a werewolf. It sucks to be a mage sometimes, it sucks to be a hunter sometimes, the fact that being a Promethean sucks is the motivating conflict of the game, it sucks to be a changeling... or at least become a changeling. It kind of sucks to be a Demon and it kind of sucks to be a Mummy. It kind of sucks to be a beast unless you're very good at finding alternative feeding methods or you're an asshole, and you can tell just from the previews that it sucks to be a Deviant. Every last one of those splats has a good reason to be all angsty about what they are.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters do not. Sin-Eaters, actually reading the book, when they're not laying spirits to rest, banishing murderous specters, or using their powers to earn some cash, they're <u><b><i>partying.</i></b></u> They're celebrating. One of the Archetypes is <i>literally </i>all about partying. They are living life to the fullest and enjoying every last second of it. That's what Sin-Eater culture is about. If that's the culture, then it's reasonable to conclude that the vast majority of Sin-Eaters, well, if they don't like their awesome powers and the fact that it's very hard for them to die, they at the very least don't regret making the bargain.<br /> <br /> And why would they? They're not dead, and there are no major drawbacks.<br /> <br /> So, think of it this way: Instead of saying that the Geist should be able to posses the Sin-Eater or otherwise punish them in a way other than lower synergy(which would be major draw backs, which Sin-Eaters lacking is a feature, not a bug,) you should ask yourself this: Why, why is this alien super ghost so willing to give up their freedom to someone else, just to live again, when they have no way to make the host keep their end of the deal once it's over, other than lying to them or hoping that the host is week willed enough to bully into compliance? Is it because such a deal is literally the only way thy can feel alive again? Is it because there are rules that compel them to make deals so unbalanced in the mortal's favor? Or is it because bad things happened to the first geist who tried to force a bargain under it's terms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T17:31:52-07:00","id":965358,"title":"","content":"1e geists couldn't possess stuff, but 2e can since they're ghosts. They can claim &amp; possess living creatures. Though the bound are very different from just a possessed or claimed individual so there is no reason that &quot;Geists can possess things&quot; should equal &quot;Geists can possess their bound&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 09-07-2016, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T19:34:43-07:00","id":965427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965289#post965289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing: Geists do not posses their hosts. The bargain is<b> explicitly not posses</b>. This is stated, flat out, in the introduction. The closest thing to possesion is the host <i>reverse </i>possesing their geist,</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know that the Bargain is not the same as possession. It is symbiosis. That does imply that there's something in it for both parties. Watching the world through the eyes of another, unable to have any influence whatsoever in the world, sounds more like a prison than a vicarious life. And if the host can reverse possess the geist, even if there isn't prior support for it, it doesn't seem beyond possibility that it might be able to go the other way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965289#post965289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the geist can posses you, the geist <i>will </i>posses you. You can't play a character like the example host of the burning woman or the woman who keeps a serial killer locked up in her soul, because the geist will just flat out posses you if you don't set your enemies on fire or go out and randomly kill people. And that sucks worse than Prometheans, because Prometheans at least have a way out of their &quot;the world itself literally hates you&quot; state.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would depend a lot on the Bargain in question. If the geist said, &quot;I'll bring you back, but in exchange, I get to come with and you need to burn some shit or watch a good fire every now and then,&quot; then the Sin-Eater would be totally in accordance with the terms of the Bargain simply by using fire to solve the problems where it was convenient, or watching a bonfire, and not need to worry about the geist getting too pissed off. On the other hand, if the terms of the agreement were &quot;I'll bring you back, but in exchange, I get to come with and you need to burn your enemies,&quot; it seems odd that not burning the enemies would have precious little in the way of consequences. This is especially true for experienced geists. &quot;Of course I'll burn my enemies if you give me another chance at sweet, sweet, life... I'm alive again? Sweet! Ha, ha, you stupid ghost, you really thought I'd do that? Thanks for the second chance, sucker!&quot; To which the geist would simply have to snap her fingers and say, &quot;Gosh darn it, you dying mortals keep pulling this, and I keep falling for it. Enjoy your super powers while they last, because I probably won't give you a third chance.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965289#post965289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, and I've said this before, but it makes <b>no sense </b>for the Geist to be able to posses it's host. If Geists had the power to posses mortals at all, then why would they even bother with the Bargain? They would just posses any convenient mortal and ride them until they broke down. The fact that they make the Bargain instead of posssing mortals tells me that they can't posses mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been confirmed that they can. This implies that there has to be something juicy about the Bargain that makes it a better option than just possessing a mortal and doing what they want. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965289#post965289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, actually reading the book, the vast Majority of Sin-Eaters are not all angsty like other splats--It sucks to be a Vampire. It sucks to be a werewolf. It sucks to be a mage sometimes, it sucks to be a hunter sometimes, the fact that being a Promethean sucks is the motivating conflict of the game, it sucks to be a changeling... or at least become a changeling. It kind of sucks to be a Demon and it kind of sucks to be a Mummy. It kind of sucks to be a beast unless you're very good at finding alternative feeding methods or you're an asshole, and you can tell just from the previews that it sucks to be a Deviant. Every last one of those splats has a good reason to be all angsty about what they are.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters do not. Sin-Eaters, actually reading the book, when they're not laying spirits to rest, banishing murderous specters, or using their powers to earn some cash, they're <u><b><i>partying.</i></b></u> They're celebrating. One of the Archetypes is <i>literally </i>all about partying. They are living life to the fullest and enjoying every last second of it. That's what Sin-Eater culture is about. If that's the culture, then it's reasonable to conclude that the vast majority of Sin-Eaters, well, if they don't like their awesome powers and the fact that it's very hard for them to die, they at the very least don't regret making the bargain.<br /> <br /> And why would they? They're not dead, and there are no major drawbacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't need to have everything perfect in order to celebrate life. There are a hell of a lot of mortals in both the real world and the Chronicles of Darkness that are absolutely ecstatic to be alive, despite all the drawbacks that come with the mortal condition. I've never seen the Sin-Eater culture of celebrating life to mean that they are completely free of downsides. I've always seen it as something where they celebrate life because, despite all the bad things, possibly even because of them in some situations, living is worth it. The good and the bad, the beautiful and the ugly, all of it together is something miraculous and wonderful and all too brief. They live life to the fullest and enjoy every last second of it, as you said. I just think that it is in spite of their troubles rather than because they don't have any. I'm not saying that they shouldn't feel that the Bargain was a good idea. I'm not saying that the good shouldn't outweigh the bad. I'm saying that in the grand scheme of things, it should still be something where some would be happy with it and some would have regrets. Every entity in the Chronicles of Darkness has some things that could be seen as a downside. All of them have some good and some bad. Sin-Eaters should be no different in that regard. If some all powerful genie shows up and offers to transform a person into a Sin-Eater, then it doesn't seem very fitting in the horror genre to have it be something where only a moron would even hesitate to accept. There should be pros and cons to weigh, not simply an offer of &quot;Hey, how would you like me to take away all of your weaknesses, replace them with more advantages and super powers, enough to stand side by side with any other supernatural creature and hold your own? What's the catch you say? Well, that's the best part. There isn't one. You get all that, no strings attached. Unlike all those other fools out there, you don't even have a weakness to balance out your new strengths. Well, okay, you'll have a creepy ghost with you, and it might pout, but the worst you'll have to deal with is an earworm.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965289#post965289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, think of it this way: Instead of saying that the Geist should be able to posses the Sin-Eater or otherwise punish them in a way other than lower synergy(which would be major draw backs, which Sin-Eaters lacking is a feature, not a bug,) you should ask yourself this: Why, why is this alien super ghost so willing to give up their freedom to someone else, just to live again, when they have no way to make the host keep their end of the deal once it's over, other than lying to them or hoping that the host is week willed enough to bully into compliance? Is it because such a deal is literally the only way thy can feel alive again? Is it because there are rules that compel them to make deals so unbalanced in the mortal's favor? Or is it because bad things happened to the first geist who tried to force a bargain under it's terms?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is exactly my point. Why should a geist want to enter into a relationship like this if they're going to be giving all their power to someone with no reason to support their interests? Why should this extremely potent ghost choose to become a prisoner in someone else's head with no way to influence anything? I don't think that this exchange should be the default:<br /> <br /> Geist: Okay, you're about to die. You don't have to. I'll allow you to live again, in exchange for x, y, and z.<br /> Sin-Eater: Okay, agreed.<br /> G: It is done. You are alive, and x is now fulfilled.<br /> SE: Great. This is awesome.<br /> G: Okay, now for y and z.<br /> SE: Yeah, those aren't happening.<br /> G: But, you made a deal...<br /> SE: My promises are worth less than toilet paper, dumbass.<br /> G: If you don't hold up your end of the deal, I'll make you suffer...<br /> SE: How?<br /> G: Well, if you die again, I might not bring you back a second time.<br /> SE: Oh well. I have a second chance at life already, and thanks to these super powers you gave me, it's not going to be easy to die a second time.<br /> G: Ah.... Well, then I have other ways of making your life miserable...<br /> SE: No you don't. One of my friends is actually a Sin-Eater, and he told me all about it a couple years ago. You can't do jack shit.<br /> G: Crap. You're right.<br /> SE: Yeah. Screw you, you stupid ghost.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that Sin-Eaters should be unable to refuse their geists. Hell, I'm not even saying that they shouldn't be able to blow off their ends of the Bargains. I'm saying that there should be advantages for Sin-Eaters working in accordance with their geists, and disadvantages for ones working at odds against them. Even if possession wasn't one of them, there should be something that makes a Sin-Eater think twice before telling his or her geist to fuck off. Maybe the geist can call the attention of malicious ghosts to the Sin-Eater. Maybe it could disrupt the plasm flows in the blood, causing confusion. Maybe the earworm is bad enough that the Sin-Eater will suffer penalties to concentration. Maybe instead of full possession, the geist could cause a limb to lash out at an inopportune moment. I just think that low Synergy should be something that a Sin-Eater would want to avoid, but might accept instead of the alternative.<br /> <br /> I have often felt that a lot of the horror in Geist came from the answer to the question, &quot;What would you do for another chance at life? What sacrifices would you make? What would you agree to?&quot; If the Bargain has no teeth, then the answer to that question doesn't truly matter. Agree to whatever you wish, because you don't need to carry through. The geists are nothing but paper tigers with two major abilities - the power to take an ordinary dying mortal and transform them into the one type of entity in the entire Chronicles of Darkness that are completely lacking in any form of downside, and the power to be mildly to extremely annoying, depending on the individual. In my opinion, any Bargain that has that kind of power should be something one hesitates to break, not something that is upheld or broken casually depending on the whim of the moment.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T19:50:47-07:00","id":965436,"title":"","content":"Why do people assume that the bargain includes the geist being able to add in conditions? I mean, it's a metaphysical thing, there is no reason to assume that geists can stretch it to that extent.<br /> <br /> Also, geists do get a benefit in just hanging around inside the sin-eater. They don't get dragged back through an avernian gate and sent back to world of constant frustration and lack of fulfillment. They have no anchors so they can't exist in the mortal world or long, even if they can possess people/objects/corpses temporarily. People who die in the right threshold are the closest thing the geist has to an anchor, and once you turn them into a sin-eater they last a lot more than a geist just bleeding essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 09-07-2016, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T20:34:54-07:00","id":965453,"title":"","content":"Geists always had the ability to possess the Bound. They did it before at Synergy 0.<br /> <br /> As for choosing Bargain over Possess or Claim, all geists have Bargain apparently so there is that. Possess allows control of a body in exchange for losing all ghost powers. Claim add to Possess the ability to use Influences and power up the body. The Bargain gives a powerful ally that can be coerced into finishing the geist's business which is kind of the whole reason ghosts exist in the first place and geists are more obsessive than normal. The Bound acts like an anchor to keep the geist out of the Underworld. Even if the geist loses all their ghost powers like when Possessing, the Sin-eater is probably more capable than the geist. The Bargain seems like a good option and definitely the best choice when time is of the essence to pick one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 09-07-2016, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T20:41:48-07:00","id":965456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965453#post965453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geists always had the ability to possess the Bound. They did it before at Synergy 0.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was relatively clear that we weren't talking about the Wretched. <br /> <br /> The issue is whether they can possess Bound before they become Wretched, and if lowering Synergy (bringing the Bound closer to becoming wretched) is the only method of the geist imposing their will on the Bound's actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T20:53:34-07:00","id":965460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965456#post965456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was relatively clear that we weren't talking about the Wretched.<br /> <br /> The issue is whether they can possess Bound before they become Wretched, and if lowering Synergy (bringing the Bound closer to becoming wretched) is the only method of the geist imposing their will on the Bound's actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if Rater was excluding the Wretched. It didn't seem that way to me.<br /> <br /> Claim doesn't allow further manifestation effects so the Bargain could be in the same boat. No way to know until we are told.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 09-07-2016, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T22:41:30-07:00","id":965504,"title":"","content":"I can't help but think that this argument is becoming rather circular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T01:07:59-07:00","id":965549,"title":"","content":"Your geist can't possess you as part of the Bargain in 2e. That said, they're also emphatically not 100% under your control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T01:41:19-07:00","id":965557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965549#post965549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your geist can't possess you as part of the Bargain in 2e. That said, they're also emphatically not 100% under your control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to hear. Can't wait to hear how they influence their bound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T02:11:56-07:00","id":965562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965549#post965549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your geist can't possess you as part of the Bargain in 2e. That said, they're also emphatically not 100% under your control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for letting us know. I can't wait to see what kind of tricks they've got up their sleeves to get their way, especially since Derangements are no longer a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":". 09-08-2016, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T07:34:33-07:00","id":965661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965562#post965562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for letting us know. I can't wait to see what kind of tricks they've got up their sleeves to get their way, especially since Derangements are no longer a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if the Bargain is more like Fettering than Claiming, at least in an Unfetter option, then they could take things into their own ectoplasmic hands/claws/tentacles if the Sin-Eater isn't keeping up their end. Or just make life indirectly miserable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T08:15:11-07:00","id":965689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965427#post965427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is exactly my point. Why should a geist want to enter into a relationship like this if they're going to be giving all their power to someone with no reason to support their interests? Why should this extremely potent ghost choose to become a prisoner in someone else's head with no way to influence anything? I don't think that this exchange should be the default:</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Keep in mind that geists are ghosts that willingly gave up all but the least bit of their humanity in order to escape the Underworld.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Maybe, just maybe, being in the underworld sucks so bad that the geist who gave up their mortal identity to get out is willing to give up most of their freedom and take the risk that they're host isn't going to complete their goals in order to mimimize their chances of getting sent </span></span></span><i>back </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">to that near-literal hell</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">? I mean, at least inside the Sin-Eater they get to feel alive again, so it's already better than the Underworld.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Regardless, since the Bargain is<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965460#post965460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if Rater was excluding the Wretched. It didn't seem that way to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you go back and read some of my earlier posts, I was explicitly excluding the Wretched.<br /> <br /> The Wretched are a punishment for you screwing up and dying a lot., not a punishment for you refusing to go along with whatever immoral r illegal thing your geists might want you to do.<br /> <br /> The Argument is that, in One E, a Sin-Eater could completly ignore what their geist wanted and only suffer lower syngery for it.<br /> <br /> Some people think that the Geist should be able to posses the Sin-Eater or otherwise take control of the Sin-Eater's actions in order to force it's host to act in a certain way. I think that this is stupid. That's a source of Spernatural Angst, and one of Geists selling points is that it had almost no supernatural angst. Most Sin-Eaters are happy.<br /> <br /> I feel that if you want a mechanic for the geist Influancing the hosts, it should happen in a way that actually makes sense with how the Bond Works. The Bond is symbiosis and it doesn't happen unless the mortal half consents. So the Bargain woudld have to be better than dying(and if a murder ghost can posses you whenever the hell it wonts then dying is better) and it has to be mutually beneficial.<br /> <br /> And the geist doen'st need to be able to posses the host or punish them to be mutually beneficial: Te host gets to live and gets super powers. The geist to experiance the sensations of life and can't b destroyed as long as it's bound.(which I sort of just remembered)<br /> <br /> So any mechanic should be symbiotic--Sin-Eaters that do things that their geists like and get along with them are rewarded with more opportunities to regain will power or recharge their plasm or get beats so they're stronger in general than Sin-Eaters who don't get along with their Geists, who also have lower synergy.<br /> <br /> Also, I figured that if a Geist had a specific agenda it would just wait on a host that fit the agenda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 09-08-2016, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T08:35:52-07:00","id":965699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965689#post965689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some people think that the Geist should be able to posses the Sin-Eater or otherwise take control of the Sin-Eater's actions in order to force it's host to act in a certain way. I think that this is stupid. That's a source of Spernatural Angst, and one of Geists selling points is that it had almost no supernatural angst. Most Sin-Eaters are happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are these selling points listed, again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T11:22:32-07:00","id":965760,"title":"","content":"Sorry, Rater. I must have missed it in all the back and forth. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I was actually under the impression that a Sin-Eater couldn't be possessed because they kind of already were. Switching from Bound to Possessed or Claimed seems like a downgrade. Since the Bound was the player, not the geist, it would not make sense to me for the game to allow a ST to take control of a player's character because they didn't do what the ST wanted. I don't find other reasons compelling though. I guess it doesn't matter since Geists can't Possess their Bound.<br /> <br /> The Bargain has to include the Bound helping the geist do whatever it needs to do in the mortal world. Otherwise, it should be called the Gift. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm not sure a geist would know what it needs done precisely though. Even if a geist can punish the Bound it isn't going to come up often if the geist only gives vague directions. It will work out so there is no need to worry about it.<br /> <br /> I still think having to deal with ghosts provides angst but I guess if someone doesn't think that rises to the level necessary then angst free it is. Sin-Eaters were never depicted particularly happy but they certainly were grateful to be alive (close to the same thing). Better to live with ghosts than become one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T15:26:06-07:00","id":965899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965699#post965699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where are these selling points listed, again?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In the game.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It's what the game is about. Why play Geist over Vampire or Changeling? Becuase it doen'st suck to b a Sin-Eater. Sin-Eaters, forthe most part, seem to like what they are or at the very least don't hate it.<br /> <br /> giving them a reason to hate making the Bargain diminishes that, and diminsishes one of the thigns that makes Geist distinct from the other gamelines.<br /> <br /> It'd be like taking dream stuff out of changeling.</span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965760#post965760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bargain has to include the Bound helping the geist do whatever it needs to do in the mortal world. Otherwise, it should be called the Gift. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm not sure a geist would know what it needs done precisely though. Even if a geist can punish the Bound it isn't going to come up often if the geist only gives vague directions. It will work out so there is no need to worry about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't.<br /> <br /> The Mortal Gets: To not die, and awesome powers.<br /> The Geist gets: To experience the sensations of being alive and not have to worry about being forced back into the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Mortal Loses: Privacy, they will never be alone even when they want to be and they might not get along with thier new head guest.<br /> Geist Loses: Agency, they can yell and scream, but they can not do anything to force their host to do anything.<br /> <br /> That seems like a fair deal to me.<br /> <br /> Anything the geist wants beyond making the Bargain is them asking a favor after the fact. The host should be free to refuse such favors, but refusing to many too often or refusing even the most innocuous should result in low synergy(because your geist hates you, not because it's punishing you), and doing the favors should result in a reward of some kind--regain expended will power, recharge your plasma, extra beats. Something rewarding, because the Geist isn't a malevolent possessing entity, nor is it a parasite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 09-08-2016, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T16:00:48-07:00","id":965907,"title":"","content":"Remember where Chronicles of Darkness is a horror game? Geist needs some of that, and it can't be all external.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T17:34:50-07:00","id":965944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965907#post965907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember where Chronicles of Darkness is a horror game? Geist needs some of that, and it can't be all external.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... because &quot;Geists aren't able to force you to murder people&quot; =! no personal horror?<br /> <br /> You're still chained to an insane ghost, you have to deal with echoes of people who are trapped in a horrible cycle and cannot move forward, you have to deal with seeing and hearing horrific things, you have to deal with the relatives who are left behind, you have to deal with the fact that even if you accept your own death and are content you Can't die without either being 80-100 years old or having your soul torn up until you are a husk, as you get more you even need spend time down in the horrible depths of the underworld, instead of trying to be mentally balanced you're drawn to and encouraged and become more symbiotic with a mind that is innately alien.<br /> <br /> I can see personal horror resulting in having to deal with those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T19:59:50-07:00","id":966005,"title":"","content":"How about the fact that ghosts know what you are, that you can't stop feeling ghosts use their numina, and that the stronger you are the harder it is to turn off your ghost senses? That seems like a horror, even if it's one from an outsider's perspective; from within it, it seems like it'd be kind of numbing, if not depressing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T20:47:33-07:00","id":966021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965944#post965944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.... because &quot;Geists aren't able to force you to murder people&quot; =! no personal horror?<br /> <br /> You're still chained to an insane ghost, you have to deal with echoes of people who are trapped in a horrible cycle and cannot move forward, you have to deal with seeing and hearing horrific things, you have to deal with the relatives who are left behind, you have to deal with the fact that even if you accept your own death and are content you Can't die without either being 80-100 years old or having your soul torn up until you are a husk, as you get more you even need spend time down in the horrible depths of the underworld, instead of trying to be mentally balanced you're drawn to and encouraged and become more symbiotic with a mind that is innately alien.<br /> <br /> I can see personal horror resulting in having to deal with those things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly the point I wanted to make. The Bound get to a second chance at life, sure, but it is at the cost of an alien passenger living inside of your head/soul and even if they can't force you to do anything or make your life as bad as the Shadow did in <i>Wraith</i>, it's not &quot;oh boy, this is awesome!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T21:19:05-07:00","id":966031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966021#post966021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly the point I wanted to make. The Bound get to a second chance at life, sure, but it is at the cost of an alien passenger living inside of your head/soul and even if they can't force you to do anything or make your life as bad as the Shadow did in <i>Wraith</i>, it's not &quot;oh boy, this is awesome!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Except I'd still want most Bound to have the view of &quot;oh boy, this is awesome!&quot;. Even if I don't think Geist's selling point isn't &quot;It's not angsty&quot;, my view is that it's selling point is &quot;Just because the world is a horrific horrible place, doesn't mean life isn't amazing, beautiful, and awesome!&quot; (which is basically just a fancy way of saying It's not angsty I guess *shrug*). Just because it's a horror game, doesn't mean it should be a Wraith-y angsty borefest that sees death so grimly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 09-09-2016, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T22:11:59-07:00","id":966052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966031#post966031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except I'd still want most Bound to have the view of &quot;oh boy, this is awesome!&quot;. Even if I don't think Geist's selling point isn't &quot;It's not angsty&quot;, my view is that it's selling point is &quot;Just because the world is a horrific horrible place, doesn't mean life isn't amazing, beautiful, and awesome!&quot; (which is basically just a fancy way of saying It's not angsty I guess *shrug*). Just because it's a horror game, doesn't mean it should be a Wraith-y angsty borefest that sees death so grimly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think calling Wraith an &quot;angsty borefest&quot; is necessary, speaking as someone who was saved from suicidal depression by it.<br /> <br /> By all mines, allow the Bound to be celebrants! Let them revel in having a second shot at doing things right! But what I don't want is a game where you're a normal person brought back to life with death-themed superpowers who sometimes punches ghosts and also you have an insane undead spirit that lives in your head but doesn't negatively impact you whatsoever. Geist 1e has a similar slip-up as a bad Mage chronicle in that it has a nasty tendency to feel like urban fantasy with a spooky coat of paint instead of something that has a place alongside Vampire and Changeling.<br /> <br /> The Geist needs mechanical teeth to it. Don't make the Bound regret making the Bargain - because hey, they aren't dead anymore - but don't make it a game of voodoo superheroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T23:03:52-07:00","id":966075,"title":"","content":"I don't know that geists get to feel the sensations of being alive. The Bound being alive and the Geist not going to the underworld is a fair trade. The Bound getting power and the geist not getting help with the thing that was important enough for the geist to do something crazy by ghost standards, which is really an all-consuming focus for the geist, doesn't seem fair at all. The Bound should be agreeing to work towards the Geist's goals as part of the Bargain, but I would think if the Bound says screw it then Synergy loss or risk should be sufficient. I don't know what the goals Geist's have at this point though. The Bound saying &quot;screw it&quot; is a very different thing than I'll get to it later so I'm not suggesting they should be treated the same.<br /> <br /> I was thinking the &quot;celebrate being alive&quot; was because of the Bound rather than the Geist and, if not, then it should be. If a Geist wanted sensations then they should just possess or claim somebody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T23:37:21-07:00","id":966083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966075#post966075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know that geists get to feel the sensations of being alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>They explicitly do.<br /> <br /> Geister are pretty much by definition made from ghosts who have an abiding interest in the mortal world, and between conventional literature about dead men whose meals all taste of ash (to say nothing of how dismal the state of Twilight is) and the Underworld overflowing with all manner of better-than-you-ever-got-when-you-were-alive temptations, they're rather distinctly in a position to want to experience Life in a fashion that doesn't inherently remind them of how monstrous they've become.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a Geist wanted sensations then they should just possess or claim somebody. </div> </div> </div>There is a significant operative difference between being a living human person and being an entropic wreck crammed into a meat-suit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T23:48:03-07:00","id":966089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966083#post966083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a significant operative difference between being a living human person and being an entropic wreck crammed into a meat-suit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I've always taken Possesion to imply a certain detachment from the host, like the entity's the driver, looking out of the windscreen and so on, rather than actually <i>being</i> the person (or experiencing it that way). Claiming is closer, but it still warps the body away from the human, making it pretty darn difficult to live a normal (ish) human life, like most geists want to remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T02:28:31-07:00","id":966119,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen anything to suggest what level of sensation an ephemeral being has when manifesting Possession or Claim. I had to read through half the book to find a line buried in the text to suggest geists feel human and desire it. Assuming this is not an embellishment by a single writer it is used to explain why Sin-Eaters don't fall unconscious from wounds not given as a reason for wanting to enter a Bargain. The reason repeatedly given is geists want to affect the mortal world and desire the most powerful vessel to do so. They give up control for power. The geist can't force the bound to act according to its will but a player's geist shouldn't be crazy enough to not have the Bargain include working the geist's goals.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, it would seem a Sin-Eater's geist would be represented by Aspirations. When a player chooses to defy a geist aspiration the character suffers a breaking point. Whether these breaking points are listed in the book as standard or optional and a ST decides to remove them or the breaking points are absent and added by a ST, it seems to me the game is the same either way. The game differs in a minor, although perhaps significant, way on a table by table basis which literally is every game that comes out. Nobody makes games that everybody thinks are perfect out of the box.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T06:02:08-07:00","id":966162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965899#post965899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In the game.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Page number?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965899#post965899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]It's what the game is about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could have sworn it was about ghost stories and second chances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965899#post965899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why play Geist over Vampire or Changeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>See above?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965899#post965899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">giving them a reason to hate making the Bargain diminishes that, and diminsishes one of the thigns that makes Geist distinct from the other gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean, playing a mortal psychopomp given a second chance at life is something the other gamelines all give you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=965899#post965899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd be like taking dream stuff out of changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, you <i>can</i> and it is still a strong, worth while game. Changeling isn't about dreams themselves (though it can and does feature them, obviously).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T09:52:50-07:00","id":966289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966162#post966162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page number?</div> </div> </div> </div>Too many to name.<br /> <br /> Read the book, particularly the sections on what it means to be a Sin-Eater and on Sin-Eater Culture. These individuals are happy.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966162#post966162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean, playing a mortal psychopomp given a second chance at life is something the other gamelines all give you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, don't make a straw man out of me.<br /> <br /> I said <b>one</b> of the things that makes it distinct... Though a Mage with a specialty in Death Arcanum could probably do the Psychopomp thing pretty well, and I'm pretty sure that every most splats have at least one way to interact with ghosts.<br /> <br /> One of the points of Geist is that the Sin-Eaters, for the most part, are happy with what they are... Or at the very least don't regret it. They aren't angsty like young Vampires are sometimes, and they really have no reason to. The Bargain is a great deal. Most sin-eaters have no reason to regret it, and that lets them you know, actually <i>enjoy </i>their second chance.<br /> <br /> Because there's no point in having a second chance if you can't actually enjoy it or use it or if it's worse than your first chance--if you regret your second chance, then you're doing it wrong.<br /> <br /> So, don't give Sin-Eaters a reason to regret their second chance.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966162#post966162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funnily enough, you <i>can</i> and it is still a strong, worth while game. Changeling isn't about dreams themselves (though it can and does feature them, obviously).</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's not a s unique anymore, compared to the rest of the Chronicles, is it? No, it's not. You've made it more similar to the others.<br /> <br /> Every game line past has something that makes it distinct, beyond it's main themes.<br /> <br /> Taking &quot;You know, being a Sin-Eater really in'st that bad. It's actually kind of awesome.&quot; makes Geist less distinct compared to the other game lines.<br /> <br /> Does Vampire really need you to worry about the political scheming of the Elders? No, but dropping it lessens the game a bit.<br /> Does Werewolf really need the conflict between the Forsaken and the Pure when you've already got hostile and alien spirits to deal with?? No, but removing it lessens the game a bit.<br /> Does Mage really need Paradox and the complications it causes? Not really, there are plenty of reasons already to keep hidden, but dropping it makes the game a bit less than it is.<br /> Does Promethean really need it's built in Happy Ending? No, but taking away the fact that it's totally possible for a Promethean to escape their living hell lessens the game.<br /> Does Hunter Really need it's competing Anti-Monster conspiracies? No, it's perfectly valid to play it starting at tier one and staying there, but not having the option to mess around with the Conspiracies lessens the game a bit.<br /> Does Changeling really need to have the ability to mess around with dreams and dream imagery? No, but it's fun to have.<br /> Does Mummy really need to have you start at the top of the heap and slowly degrade back down? No, but it's pretty fucking cool.<br /> Does Demon really need to be the cover's mechanic instead of just having the one cover you maintain? No, but without it you're just playing a more extreme version of the espionage that comes in a political maneuvering game of Vampire or the Conspiracy conflict based game of Hunter.<br /> Foes beat really need to be crossover compatible right out of the box? No, you can have fun playing a troll or a dragon or a kraken, but the crossover stuff is fun to have.<br /> <br /> Does Geist absolutely need to be the game with little to no Supernatural Angst? No. But it's pretty fucking fun and it's something that Geist has that the others don't have by default.<br /> <br /> So, let's keep it. It adds something to the game that the others don't have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 09-09-2016, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T10:32:08-07:00","id":966313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966289#post966289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too many to name.<br /> <br /> Read the book, particularly the sections on what it means to be a Sin-Eater and on Sin-Eater Culture. These individuals are happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have. Twice. It never says &quot;here's why you should play/buy Geist: the Sin-Eaters - there's no Angst!&quot;. That's your inference. It's a common one based on the reading of the rules, granted, but it is not, I think, a baked-in &quot;selling point&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966289#post966289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, don't make a straw man out of me.<br /> <br /> I said <b>one</b> of the things that makes it distinct... Though a Mage with a specialty in Death Arcanum could probably do the Psychopomp thing pretty well, and I'm pretty sure that every most splats have at least one way to interact with ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages can dabble, but they are more research and less &quot;living with ghosts&quot;. A Moros <i>can</i> do some of what Sin-Eaters do, but not with the same focus, and it is only one part of their wheelhouse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966289#post966289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the points of Geist is that the Sin-Eaters, for the most part, are happy with what they are... Or at the very least don't regret it. They aren't angsty like young Vampires are sometimes, and they really have no reason to. The Bargain is a great deal. Most sin-eaters have no reason to regret it, and that lets them you know, actually <i>enjoy </i>their second chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they still <i>can</i>. Literally nothing proposed (even the rare Geist possession) really takes away that the Bargain is an awesome deal. What people have problems with is that it is all plus, no negatives. In a Horror game. About ghosts. It strains disbelief that it is entirely one-sided. Just because one might have to do something <i>that they agreed to</i>, in no way invalidates their second chance at life, nor the awesome powers they get.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966289#post966289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because there's no point in having a second chance if you can't actually enjoy it or use it or if it's worse than your first chance--if you regret your second chance, then you're doing it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>As above, they still can. Just because you didn't get ice in your drink doesn't mean a whole meal is crap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966289#post966289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, don't give Sin-Eaters a reason to regret their second chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's <i>reducing</i> the potential stories that can be told. Everyone should get a chance to regret. I mean, the game is based around regret. Even Sin-Eaters should be able to indulge, to varying degrees of justification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966289#post966289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's not a s unique anymore, compared to the rest of the Chronicles, is it? No, it's not. You've made it more similar to the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Horror game. Universal themes. They all use the same base mechanics, don't they? Commonality is not an automatic negative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966289#post966289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Geist absolutely need to be the game with little to no Supernatural Angst? No. But it's pretty fucking fun and it's something that Geist has that the others don't have by default.<br /> <br /> So, let's keep it. It adds something to the game that the others don't have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, no one is proposing to turn it into Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:39:02-07:00","id":966386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966313#post966313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they still <i>can</i>. Literally nothing proposed (even the rare Geist possession) really takes away that the Bargain is an awesome deal. What people have problems with is that it is all plus, no negatives. In a Horror game. About ghosts. It strains disbelief that it is entirely one-sided. Just because one might have to do something <i>that they agreed to</i>, in no way invalidates their second chance at life, nor the awesome powers they get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Instead of saying that the Bargain shoudlnt be one sided, you should ask why the Bargain is one sided?<br /> <br /> <b>Why </b>is the Geist willing to give up it's freedom to a mortal who might refuse to do anything it wants? Why is it willing to risk becoming a prisoner in someone elses head, with only the ability to reward the host for doing things it likes and scream and curse impotently when the host refuses it to enforce their will?<br /> <br /> Maybe, just maybe, being a host that is so old and so twisted that it can no longer remember being human, let alone what it feels like to be alive, who can only escape from the bleak and boring and banal underworld for a short period of time otherwise is just that much <i>worse </i>than surrendering their agency to a mortal?<br /> <br /> Maybe the horror comes less from &quot;what are you, a mortal, willing to do to live again&quot; and more from &quot;how bad does being dead suck if the dead are willing to give up their sanity and humanity to escape it and their freedom to feel alive again?&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is a totally valid theme to explore.I mean, there are vampires and Mages who enslave the dead--probably specialists from other splats as well, all kinds of beings literally eat ghosts, and the Underworld is a cold, dark, and scary placed ruled by mad beings that were never human and are concerned only that their insane and sometimes contradictory laws are followed.<br /> <br /> I'd <i>gladly</i> becomes the voice in the back of someone's head to get the hell away from that. Play up the horror of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Now, you want an inherent downside to being a Sin-Eater? Fine, just don't pick something that gives them reason to regret making the bargain, because if the majority of Sin-Eaters regret the Bargain, then the theme of second chances and enjoying life while you're alive is reduced greatly.<br /> <br /> Maybe weapons imbued with Anti-Ghost properties are more effective against Sin-Eaters than normal, or maybe they have trouble operating in places that Ghosts can't enter.<br /> <br /> Or maybe, just maybe, give them negatives that are <i>not </i>inherent downsides to being a Sin-Eater?<br /> <br /> I mean, ghosts will not leave you the fuck alone because they know you can see them and want you to help them finish their unfinished business.<br /> you either have to get used to it or you've got to learn how to make anti-ghost wards and put them around your residence and places of business.<br /> <br /> Statistically speaking, you <i>will </i>stumble across a place where someone died and you'll be able to tell,no matter how much you wish you didn't.<br /> <br /> You have a pretty good idea of when everyone around you is going to die. Have fun with that.<br /> <br /> Those, those are all negatives. They are not, however, permanent things. Each one can be dealt with, and seem like a far trade for having super powers and not being dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966313#post966313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's <i>reducing</i> the potential stories that can be told. Everyone should get a chance to regret. I mean, the game is based around regret. Even Sin-Eaters should be able to indulge, to varying degrees of justification.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;My geist in particular just won't shut up about *annoying, disgusting, or disturbing topic* no matter what I do. I can't think straight and I have trouble sleeping at night because of it.&quot;<br /> &quot;I really didn't need to know just how many people get murdered in my city every year. I just keep stumbling across murder scenes out while I'm out and about.&quot;<br /> &quot;The monster hunters think I'm possessed by the devil and won't leave me the hell alone. I've already been forced to kill two of them.&quot;<br /> &quot;An innocent little girl died because I screwed up and got killed while tracking down a serial killer.&quot;<br /> <br /> Boom, you've got a reason for your specific character to regret making the bargain without the Bound as a whole having a reason to regret it.<br /> <br /> Really, having a specific reason to regret the Bargain would make for a better story than &quot;here, I really don't like thi downside that all Sin-Eaters have.&quot;<br /> <br /> And again, giving<b> all </b>Sin-Eaters a reason to regret the Bargain diminishes the &quot;hey no angst&quot; bit. If it'd bad enough for one to have legitimate reason to angst, it's bad enough for most to have legitimate reason to angst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:42:20-07:00","id":966389,"title":"","content":"These are games of personal horror. Don't forget that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:50:25-07:00","id":966396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966389#post966389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are games of personal horror. Don't forget that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically what I said in my previous post--if you want to play a Sin-Eater that regrets making the Bargain or is horrified by what he is now, it makes more sense to have a personal reason than to give all Sin-Eaters a reason to angst about accepting their second chances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T13:05:03-07:00","id":966404,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I was lost in a white room. I'm back now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Are player's making characters at random? If a geist wants to kill babies then it is because a player made it so. Players should not be making characters they don't want to play. NPCs don't need mechanics to cover dealing with their geists. PCs should have Bound generally on the same page as the merged Geist.<br /> <br /> I still think Geists would be represented generally as Aspirations so it would only ever be an issue if the ST is setting them. If a player says &quot;screw it&quot; then the Aspiration changes when the Chapter ends and the character can suffer a breaking point. If the book goes in a different direction and you don't like internal angst (or whatever) then you're all set. Otherwise, you can set your level of &quot;angst&quot; by the number of Geistpirations, adding them into the game if necessary.<br /> <br /> Is the rest of the debate little more than an argument over how people want to play a game? I don't think that is productive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T13:13:18-07:00","id":966407,"title":"","content":"And having the Geist have a little leeway in no way makes &quot;all Sin-Eaters regret the Bargain&quot;. Heck, some might be gung ho in doing what the Geist wants.<br /> <br /> You seem to think Geists <i>not</i> being anything more than trivial backstory and a power source somehow makes getting to live again, superpowers, and being nigh-immortal a bad thing worthy of angst.<br /> <br /> The Geist should have a bigger impact on the character than &quot;Yeah, I made a deal with some old ghost made out of auto parts to come back to life, but now I just ignore them and enjoy the super powers. Ghosts? Ignore them too. Know when people are going to die? Short sell stock in life insurance time.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T13:59:25-07:00","id":966423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966407#post966407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And having the Geist have a little leeway in no way makes &quot;all Sin-Eaters regret the Bargain&quot;. Heck, some might be gung ho in doing what the Geist wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody said &quot;little leeway.&quot;<br /> <br /> What I've been suggestiong, and what others have suggested, that Geists can influance their hosts to do what they geist wants by giving the host rewards for doing things that the geist likes, that's a little Leeway.<br /> <br /> People are asking for the geist to be able to take over the host whenever it damn well feels like it or to be able to punish the sin-eaters if the Sin-Eater refuses to do something the geist wants even once.<br /> <br /> That is a major draw back on the level of the Beast for Vampires or Paradox for Mages. Things that give Legitimate reason to angst, and &quot;hey, most Sin-Eaters think Angsting about being what they are is silly, now, Bobby and his Krewe just helped an 80 old murder victim find piece and pass on so they're having a party, I'm bringing the rum&quot; is a pretty big part of the story.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966407#post966407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to think Geists <i>not</i> being anything more than trivial backstory and a power source somehow makes getting to live again, superpowers, and being nigh-immortal a bad thing worthy of angst.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, don't make me a straw man.<br /> Nowhere did I say anything like that.<br /> <br /> I said that if you turn the geist into a a major draw back, let it posses the host or let it punish the host severely if the host refuses to go out and murder someone in cold blood or burn down a house, or any of those unsavory things that some geists want, those are major draw backs that give the Sin-Eater reason to angst about bieing a Sin-Eater and that's a nono.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966407#post966407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Geist should have a bigger impact on the character than &quot;Yeah, I made a deal with some old ghost made out of auto parts to come back to life, but now I just ignore them and enjoy the super powers. Ghosts? Ignore them too. Know when people are going to die? Short sell stock in life insurance time.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The geist does not need the abillty to punish it's host for refusing to do what it wants to be a big inflaunce, and I've flat out cited the ghosts refusing to leave you alone(so you <b>can't </b>ignore them) and being able to tell when are going to die as donwsides, so I don't really see the point in you bringing those up.<br /> <br /> You want the Geist to be big? The Geist has it's own virtue and vice, it's own aspirations, it's own goals, and fulfilling those gives you willpower and beats, maybe plasm, as though you were fulfillin your own aspirations and virtues and vices.<br /> <br /> If you absolutely refuse to fulfill the Geists aspiration, or do even small things for it even when it asks, even if all it's saying is &quot;hey, I don't like that kind of whiskey, get that other kind&quot;congratulations, your geist <i>hates you</i>. You now have low synergy and all of the Downsides that comes from that.<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously, the Geist is part of your character. It is under your control as a Player. If you want it to be a big deal, you just have to talk in character as the geist, act out it whispering things to your Sin-Eater and making demands, and roleplay out your sin-eater giving into the demand or refusing it, and if you refuse it your geist getting mad at your Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> You do not need mechanics for that, and you especially do not need mechanics that would make being a Sin-Eater suck for that.<br /> <br /> The general assumption is that most Sin-Eaters either get along with the Geist or can control or appease it, and the fact that you can tell it to shut the fuck up if it tells you to go on a killing spree without too many consequences is a point in the game's favor. If you want to play a Sin-Eater whose geist hates him or her, or that has an agenda that your host doesn't agree with it, then you can just talk about that with the storyteller ahead of time. You do not need mechanics to enforce that, and it certainly does not need to be the default assumption of the game.<br /> <br /> Because, you know, if almost every sin-eater has a geist that wants them to do things that the Sin-Eater doen'st want to do, and if the Geist has the abillity to force the Sin-Eater to do these things, then being a Sin-Eater sucks, and the fact that being a Sin-Eater doen'st suck is one of the core things in Geist that makes it Distinct from the other gamelines.<br /> <br /> So, here we go: Maybe, since you're playing two characters, you're expected to <i>roleplay</i> two character? Does that make the Geist relevant enough?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 09-09-2016, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T05:43:09-07:00","id":966722,"title":"","content":"I'm cool with <b>Geist</b> being more hopeful and optimistic than other lines, but having an inhuman ghost from the depths of the Underworld riding in the back of your skull can't <i>all</i> be good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T10:34:25-07:00","id":966820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966722#post966722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm cool with <b>Geist</b> being more hopeful and optimistic than other lines, but having an inhuman ghost from the depths of the Underworld riding in the back of your skull can't <i>all</i> be good</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not.<br /> <br /> Other ghosts won't leave you the fuck alone and you know when all of your mortal friends and family are going to die. Those are bad things that you're going to have to learn to deal with.<br /> <br /> You're inhuman ghost partner is inhuman--you <i>will need </i>to learn how to communicate with it if you want to have a good relationship and thus fully benefit from your bond, or you'll face the consequences of low synergy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 09-10-2016, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T08:33:49-07:00","id":967332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=966820#post966820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not.<br /> <br /> Other ghosts won't leave you the fuck alone and you know when all of your mortal friends and family are going to die. Those are bad things that you're going to have to learn to deal with.<br /> <br /> You're inhuman ghost partner is inhuman--you <i>will need </i>to learn how to communicate with it if you want to have a good relationship and thus fully benefit from your bond, or you'll face the consequences of low synergy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, you can always throat punch or destroy ghosts who annoy you until they leave you alone, so that isn't much of a down side. And everyone dies, so that really isn't a downside either. Heck, knowing when lets you prevent it or at the very least know how much time you do have so nothing is left unsaid.<br /> <br /> And you can always tell your inhuman passenger to shut it and ignore them, since that doesn't have any consequences outside of low rolls on some actions, or until you hit 0 Synergy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:44:51-07:00","id":967471,"title":"","content":"And how long do you think it'll take to hit 0 synergy if your geist<i> <b><u>hates</u></b> </i>you? When you can't sleep at night because it's constantly yelling and screaming and cursing about how much it hates you?<br /> <br /> you don't need a punishment mechanic or some way for the geist to force the host to do what it wants, becuase if you tell your geist to shut the fuck up every single time it asks you to do anything, you're <i>sprinting</i> towards Syn-0<br /> <br /> But seriously There's no need for a punishment mechanic at all. You, the player, decide your geists agenda. If you want confilfict between the host and geist ,well the Geist is part of your character. It's exactly as big a deal as you, the player, want it to be. You're <i>playing </i>two characters,<i> roleplay</i> two characters--you don't need <i>any </i>mechanics for it, especially not ones that punish you for playing one of the Example characters.<br /> <br /> I mean, the book flat out says that there are SIn-Eaters who lock up murderous geists deap int heir souls. You can't do that if the Geist can force you into doing what it wants. Hence, the giest can <i>not</i> force you to do what it wants, until you hit Syn Zero.<br /> <br /> And yes, knowing exactly when everyone around you is going to die is a downside. It's just one that you can <b>deal</b> with. Which is fitting with the themes of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T15:13:11-07:00","id":967549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967471#post967471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how long do you think it'll take to hit 0 synergy if your geist<i> <b><u>hates</u></b> </i>you? When you can't sleep at night because it's constantly yelling and screaming and cursing about how much it hates you?</div> </div> </div> </div>The geist constantly screaming sounds like a good source of negative Conditions that have actual mechanical effects. That would seem appropriate to me for consequences of low Synergy, given that Derangements are no longer a thing in second edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967471#post967471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you don't need a punishment mechanic or some way for the geist to force the host to do what it wants, becuase if you tell your geist to shut the fuck up every single time it asks you to do anything, you're <i>sprinting</i> towards Syn-0</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I missed it, there's no actual mechanics in first edition for losing Synergy by telling your geist to shut up. Unless, of course, your geist is requesting that you torture people less. Of course, if it is requesting that you do it more, then acting in accordance with the geist's wishes will cost you Synergy rather than opposing them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967471#post967471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But seriously There's no need for a punishment mechanic at all. You, the player, decide your geists agenda. If you want confilfict between the host and geist ,well the Geist is part of your character. It's exactly as big a deal as you, the player, want it to be. You're <i>playing </i>two characters,<i> roleplay</i> two characters--you don't need <i>any </i>mechanics for it, especially not ones that punish you for playing one of the Example characters.<br /> <br /> I mean, the book flat out says that there are SIn-Eaters who lock up murderous geists deap int heir souls. You can't do that if the Geist can force you into doing what it wants. Hence, the giest can <i>not</i> force you to do what it wants, until you hit Syn Zero.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm dropping the possession thing, as that has already been confirmed to not be a part of the second edition. At this point, I will be content if the geist has teeth. That doesn't prevent a character from being able to hold a murderous geist in check. It just means that they need to be willing to endure some hardship to do so, which actually makes doing so a bit more noteworthy than if it is merely a matter of ignoring the little voice. Conditions could work nicely for that, and also act as a nice source of Beats for a Sin-Eater that is trying to make the world a better place by keeping his or her psychotic geist out of trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T15:23:22-07:00","id":967555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967471#post967471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how long do you think it'll take to hit 0 synergy if your geist<i> <b><u>hates</u></b> </i>you?</div> </div> </div> </div>According the the 1E rules as they stand? Indefinitely, since Synergy Discord triggers aren't based on your Geist's personal preferences. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967471#post967471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you can't sleep at night because it's constantly yelling and screaming and cursing about how much it hates you?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd be surprised what you can tune out and get used to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967471#post967471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you don't need a punishment mechanic or some way for the geist to force the host to do what it wants, becuase if you tell your geist to shut the fuck up every single time it asks you to do anything, you're <i>sprinting</i> towards Syn-0</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is <u>not</u> a punishment mechanic, how? &quot;Do/Don't do this or you lose a Trait dot.&quot; <br /> <br /> But that's irrelevant - The text <i>talks</i> good game about how Synergy is how well they get along, but none of the triggers are about the Geist's wants or desires, just general rules for Sin-Eater actions. Open an Avernian Gate? Discord at 10. Mass murder? Discord at 1 - <i>even if your Geist is a mass murderer</i>. But tell them to F off? Not on the chart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967471#post967471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the book flat out says that there are SIn-Eaters who lock up murderous geists deap int heir souls. You can't do that if the Geist can force you into doing what it wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which only supports my point that as it stands, Geists are toothless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967471#post967471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence, the giest can <i>not</i> force you to do what it wants, until you hit Syn Zero.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, unless Synergy/Discord changes, won't happen just by disagreement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967471#post967471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, knowing exactly when everyone around you is going to die is a downside. It's just one that you can <b>deal</b> with. Which is fitting with the themes of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Highly</i> subjective as a downside. I'm not talking one that some people can learn to live with - I'm talking some would just see it as a positive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T16:02:47-07:00","id":967583,"title":"","content":"It's not letting me quote both posts, bear with me as I edit.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967549#post967549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The geist constantly screaming sounds like a good source of negative Conditions that have actual mechanical effects. That would seem appropriate to me for consequences of low Synergy, given that Derangements are no longer a thing in second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div> And it's an appropriate downside, because it ins't <i>inherent</i> to being a Sin-Eater(and thus something to angst over). It's because you're <i>bad</i> at being a Sin-Eater. The most successful sin-eaters are the ones who either get along with their geists or can find a way to vent their urges and desires into a positive direction. If you're geist hates you, you've fucked up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967549#post967549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I missed it, there's no actual mechanics in first edition for losing Synergy by telling your geist to shut up. Unless, of course, your geist is requesting that you torture people less. Of course, if it is requesting that you do it more, then acting in accordance with the geist's wishes will cost you Synergy rather than opposing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And really, that's something that should change in 2E. Synergy is supposed to be a measure of how strong the bond between you and your geist is. It should probably take your relationship with the Geist into consideration.<br /> <br /> At the very least, doing things that piss off your geist should be a Breaking Point or pretty much every Sin-Eater.&quot;<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967549#post967549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm dropping the possession thing, as that has already been confirmed to not be a part of the second edition. At this point, I will be content if the geist has teeth. That doesn't prevent a character from being able to hold a murderous geist in check. It just means that they need to be willing to endure some hardship to do so, which actually makes doing so a bit more noteworthy than if it is merely a matter of ignoring the little voice. Conditions could work nicely for that, and also act as a nice source of Beats for a Sin-Eater that is trying to make the world a better place by keeping his or her psychotic geist out of trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having to deal with low synergy and the conditions and other downsides that comes from that, and having &quot;finding some way to safely appease my geist&quot; taking up one of your aspiration spots is enough in the way of teeth. It's when the Geist can literally force the Sin-Eater to act in the Geist's wishes that &quot;keep my psychotic geist in check&quot; stops being a viable character option.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with more downsides to being a Sin-Eater, as long as the deal is still<i> ultimately</i> one sided in the Mortals Favor, because being one sided in the mortal's favor is one of the reasons why Sin-Eaters have little reason to regret it and can just go out and have fun living life. The downsides also have to be <i>appropriate, </i>logically and thematically, for the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":".  Trying and failing to combine posts 09-11-2016, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T16:10:24-07:00","id":967585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967555#post967555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that is <u>not</u> a punishment mechanic, how? &quot;Do/Don't do this or you lose a Trait dot.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Becuase <i>every </i>splat, including pure mortals, has that? You hit a breaking point, you lose a dot of Integrity/Humanity/Harmony/Wisdom/Thingy<br /> <br /> Since Synergy is a measurement of the strength of the bond between Sin-Eater and Geist, &quot;continuously ignoring your Geist's desires&quot; should be a breaking point.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But that's irrelevant - The text <i>talks</i> good game about how Synergy is how well they get along, but none of the triggers are about the Geist's wants or desires, just general rules for Sin-Eater actions. Open an Avernian Gate? Discord at 10. Mass murder? Discord at 1 - <i>even if your Geist is a mass murderer</i>. But tell them to F off? Not on the chart. </div> </div> </div>Considering that every Intergrity counterpart has changed to some degree in 2E? And really, even if telling your geist to piss off isn't a Breaking point(doing it <i>once </i>shouldn't be) You're geist <i>hating </i>you should be.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which only supports my point that as it stands, Geists are toothless. </div> </div> </div>I will gladly take &quot;Toothless geists&quot; over &quot;one of the sample concepts is unplayable&quot; because the first fits with the themes of the game to a degree while the second says that the writers weren't paying attention.<br /> <br /> And it won't let me delete this post, so it looks like I'm stuck double posting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 09-11-2016, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T16:56:15-07:00","id":967608,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you can't delete posts. It is annoying.<br /> <br /> So, basically, there is no disagreement? I might have to go back an check, but I don't think anyone said anything about your Geist randomly possessing you, or inflicting random cruelties upon you - it was always in the context of low Synergy, and outright possession is off the table anyhow. I think I proposed the &quot;Balancing the books&quot; deaths targeting your Touchstones (even incidentally) to make them personal, but that's also a &quot;only if you are stupid and get killed&quot; penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T00:46:01-07:00","id":967812,"title":"","content":"The big issue with the touchstones dying/destroyed if you die rather than a random is when you have an enemy or something your character hates as their touchstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T00:51:01-07:00","id":967814,"title":"","content":"Does Geist have a bunch of wholly-new antagonists in 2e, or should we expect a deeper drilling down into rival krewes, ghosts, necromancers, and abmortals? Can we hear more about non-Sin-Eater Bound once spoilers start properly, and if they're a purely political distinction or mechanically distinct? How important is the idea of 'archaeology' and digging into past krewes in 2e (as that was a big focus for my group when we played)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T00:55:18-07:00","id":967816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967814#post967814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Geist have a bunch of wholly-new antagonists in 2e, or should we expect a deeper drilling down into rival krewes, ghosts, necromancers, and abmortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit of both--though as I said in the other spoiler thread, ghosts are not in the Antagonists chapter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967814#post967814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we hear more about non-Sin-Eater Bound once spoilers start properly, and if they're a purely political distinction or mechanically distinct?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're one of the topics I submitted to Rose in my outline of blog entries for Geist spoilers, so yes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967814#post967814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How important is the idea of 'archaeology' and digging into past krewes in 2e (as that was a big focus for my group when we played)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hugely important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T01:11:58-07:00","id":967822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967816#post967816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A bit of both--though as I said in the other spoiler thread, ghosts are not in the Antagonists chapter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They're one of the topics I submitted to Rose in my outline of blog entries for Geist spoilers, so yes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hugely important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stellar news on all fronts. One last thing before I stop pestering you so you can go back to work on this beautiful thing: is the old thought that there's no tier 3 krewes in the world still true, and do you intend to have example or canon krewes in the book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T01:17:43-07:00","id":967826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967822#post967822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stellar news on all fronts. One last thing before I stop pestering you so you can go back to work on this beautiful thing: is the old thought that there's no tier 3 krewes in the world still true, and do you intend to have example or canon krewes in the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Answering those will have to wait for a blog post on krewes--the mechanics have changed significantly enough that talking about krewes from the context of 1e isn't really applicable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T02:26:43-07:00","id":967838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967826#post967826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Answering those will have to wait for a blog post on krewes--the mechanics have changed significantly enough that talking about krewes from the context of 1e isn't really applicable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That alone is worth just as much as a specific spoiler. I cannot wait!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T05:26:16-07:00","id":967867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967812#post967812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big issue with the touchstones dying/destroyed if you die rather than a random is when you have an enemy or something your character hates as their touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well I can see this resolved in two ways:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Just because Touchstones are <i>affected</i> by death, doesn't mean they themselves are always killed/destroyed. Something related to them might instead be the balancing sacrifice. Take a Rival as a Touchstone, and perhaps the death hits someone close to them, in a way that makes them hate you that much more.</li> <li>Feature, not a bug. If a hated Touchstone buys it, you still don't have a satisfying conclusion to that relationship, and your are still down some Anchoring facet of your existence.</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T08:00:53-07:00","id":968521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=967608#post967608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you can't delete posts. It is annoying.<br /> <br /> So, basically, there is no disagreement? I might have to go back an check, but I don't think anyone said anything about your Geist randomly possessing you, or inflicting random cruelties upon you - it was always in the context of low Synergy, and outright possession is off the table anyhow. I think I proposed the &quot;Balancing the books&quot; deaths targeting your Touchstones (even incidentally) to make them personal, but that's also a &quot;only if you are stupid and get killed&quot; penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>The disagreement is that I keep seeing people trying to make Geist Agnsty, and that's not the kind of game that geist is, so I do'n't want that.<br /> <br /> And yes, people were suggestion that geist should have some direct abillty to force you to do what they want, which is one of those things that makes Geist angsty.<br /> <br /> Hence, if you want the geist to be more relevant, to have teeth, it has to be in a way that does not, as a whole, give most sin-eaters a reason to be angsty. Becuase let's face it, that's all of the other game lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:21:41-07:00","id":978496,"title":"","content":"I don't really get where the argument that Geist is <i>the </i>game about not being angsty came from. I mean, if I were in charge of making a supplement that was cheery and upbeat, I probably wouldn't make it about dying people who spliced their souls with ghosts who exemplify the idea of death. If Geist were all about the celebration of life, why is there one archetype among eight that makes that their specific thing? Does that mean the seven-eighths who aren't Celebrants are playing wrong? And it's the World of Darkness for crying out loud. Supernatural angst is pretty much what we do. You can play the game (or any game, for that matter) whatever way you please, but saying the writers have to conform to your idea of an angst-free zone is kind of a... counterintuitive and narrow way to define the game experience?<br /> <br /> On another note, I always found it odd that Geists only get an identity when you form a Krewe. I rather prefer the idea that they cobble their identity together before they even make the Bargain. It's something I houserule in my own games, but I'm curious if that might be tweaked in the second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:34:38-07:00","id":978505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=978496#post978496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really get where the argument that Geist is <i>the </i>game about not being angsty came from. I mean, if I were in charge of making a supplement that was cheery and upbeat, I probably wouldn't make it about dying people who spliced their souls with ghosts who exemplify the idea of death. If Geist were all about the celebration of life, why is there one archetype among eight that makes that their specific thing? Does that mean the seven-eighths who aren't Celebrants are playing wrong? And it's the World of Darkness for crying out loud. Supernatural angst is pretty much what we do. You can play the game (or any game, for that matter) whatever way you please, but saying the writers have to conform to your idea of an angst-free zone is kind of a... counterintuitive and narrow way to define the game experience?<br /> <br /> On another note, I always found it odd that Geists only get an identity when you form a Krewe. I rather prefer the idea that they cobble their identity together before they even make the Bargain. It's something I houserule in my own games, but I'm curious if that might be tweaked in the second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason why people consider it <i>the</i> game to not be angsty is because there's a startling lack of reasons to be angsty. You've avoided death, you're resistant to poisons and drugs in general as well as sicknesses, and you're empowered in ways most people aren't. Even the act of coming back at all is a mutually beneficial event, because you're helping a dead being feelas alive as you literally are now. Just because you're not a Celebrant doesn't mean you're not enjoying yourself in your second lease on life either. Even Mourners, people who see themselves as still dead, enjoy their new lives in a macabre way. Celebrants are simply living life to the fullest beyond what a normal person would. Besides that, in the game book it's specified that Sin Eaters regularly hold celebrations and festivals, many of their ceremonies involve alcohol/spirits or tobacco. Their culture perpetuates enjoying life as much as it does helping the dead.<br /> <br /> Another reason Sin Eaters are a happier lot than a lot of others is because while they regularly deal with the dead, including all kinds of disturbing methods of death, they are uniquely able to completely handle these things and make them right. While they can't bring people back from the dead or fix their wounds (generally), they can help ghosts pass on peacefully, resolve last business, and take revenge in the name of the departed. They can see and hear ghosts with clarity few if any normal mortals could, they can give second chances, and if they can learn from a ghost on how to help little Suzy get her rightful inheritance then wouldn't you be happy?<br /> <br /> Also, you kind of answered your own question regarding why fans are so adherent to the idea Geist: The Sin Eaters has little inherent angst: almost every other gameline has tons of it, due in no small part to most other supernaturals having literally no choice in the matter. In becoming a Sin Eater, you may get more than you bargained for, but at least you aren't<i> dead</i>. Why make that a punishment?<br /> <br /> However, you are right; you are free to play the game however you so wish. Geists are not all saintly beings only looking out for their host's benefit, and you will not be rid of the one you have barring extreme circumstances. Ghosts know you can see them and will flock to you for it, and you can't <i>stop</i> seeing them. Heck, one of the adventure seeds is all about a Geist who drives his Sin Eater to suicide simply be endlessly repeating &quot;Dem bones dem bones will walk all over you&quot;. The gameline is full of personal horror along with grotesque, and players and storytellers can indeed tell and play angsty stories with them. It's just not the default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 09-29-2016, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T12:08:08-07:00","id":978524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=978496#post978496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really get where the argument that Geist is <i>the </i>game about not being angsty came from. I mean, if I were in charge of making a supplement that was cheery and upbeat, I probably wouldn't make it about dying people who spliced their souls with ghosts who exemplify the idea of death. If Geist were all about the celebration of life, why is there one archetype among eight that makes that their specific thing? Does that mean the seven-eighths who aren't Celebrants are playing wrong? And it's the World of Darkness for crying out loud. Supernatural angst is pretty much what we do. You can play the game (or any game, for that matter) whatever way you please, but saying the writers have to conform to your idea of an angst-free zone is kind of a... counterintuitive and narrow way to define the game experience?</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=978496#post978496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, I always found it odd that Geists only get an identity when you form a Krewe. I rather prefer the idea that they cobble their identity together before they even make the Bargain. It's something I houserule in my own games, but I'm curious if that might be tweaked in the second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is being changed in 2E. Krewe binding no longer changes a Geist's identity. If they are presenting themselves as an Angel or Baron Samedi, then they always have been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T12:29:33-07:00","id":978533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=978524#post978524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is being changed in 2E. Krewe binding no longer changes a Geist's identity. If they are presenting themselves as an Angel or Baron Samedi, then they always have been.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. Thanks for the info!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=978505#post978505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you kind of answered your own question regarding why fans are so adherent to the idea Geist: The Sin Eaters has little inherent angst: almost every other gameline has tons of it, due in no small part to most other supernaturals having literally no choice in the matter. In becoming a Sin Eater, you may get more than you bargained for, but at least you aren't<i> dead</i>. Why make that a punishment?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess because it's the World of Darkness. Nothing comes for free, and the greater the gain the steeper the price. Having a win-win splat in the WoD is really out of theme and out of tone for the franchise. If I wanted to play an upbeat game of being super awesome, I would probably go with a different setting. That's just me, though. Nothing wrong with playing it how you like.<br /> <br /> And please correct me if I'm wrong on this, but don't characters in all the major splats have the same essential choice-- supernatural life, with all its perks and drawbacks, or death? In some ways, Sin-Eaters have it worse than most... having made the Bargain, they no longer even have the option of suicide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","user":"gscrap","date":".  Edited to add response to Taidragon 09-29-2016, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:28:34-07:00","id":978579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=978533#post978533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess because it's the World of Darkness. Nothing comes for free, and the greater the gain the steeper the price. Having a win-win splat in the WoD is really out of theme and out of tone for the franchise. If I wanted to play an upbeat game of being super awesome, I would probably go with a different setting. That's just me, though. Nothing wrong with playing it how you like.<br /> <br /> And please correct me if I'm wrong on this, but don't characters in all the major splats have the same essential choice-- supernatural life, with all its perks and drawbacks, or death? In some ways, Sin-Eaters have it worse than most... having made the Bargain, they no longer even have the option of suicide.</div> </div> </div> </div>And as I noted, the price you pay is having a partly insane presence in your head constantly, the inability to stop seeing ghosts in all their grotesque states and attracting them to yourself. You can't shut your Geist up, you can't stop seeing it, and if your relationship with it deteriorates enough it becomes hostile, even outright stealing control of your body away. Any place someone has died leaves a Death Stain, which constantly gives a chilled sensation to Sin Eaters all around. Do you have any idea how hard it would be for a Sin Eater to find a decent place to live without these death stains causing problems? Trouble finds you whether you like it or not, and that is the price for being a Sin Eater.<br /> <br /> The <i>reward</i> is having a second chance at living. Again, why have angst about having a literal second chance of life, even if one with strings attached? You don't need to worry about burning at sunlight nor the task of sustaining yourself with blood; any fury that comes is inherent to yourself, not a bloodline of lycanthropy; using your powers does not cause the universe to hate you, nor are you harmed by your curiosity (anymore than a normal person); the world doesn't hate you for merely existing and trying to discover yourself; you don't have the beings who changed/created you constantly hounding you down, with anyone around you a potential backstabber (again, any more than a normal person); you don't have to hunt down creatures of the night with just your wits and a gun at your side unless you want to; you are yourself when you come back, you are not bound to collect artifacts you have few memories of, and you don't fall asleep after a set amount of time; and do not cause humans problems by merely existing because you have a horror hunger.<br /> <br /> Simply put, being a Sin Eater is not a walk in the park, but it's nice being able to play a splat whose existence doesn't suck in some innate way. If that's not your thing, you're under no obligation to play the game. However, if you're interested in having a second chance wrapped in the macabre, why not enjoy it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:02:13-07:00","id":978604,"title":"","content":"I find it curious that many posters list inherent drawbacks of being a Sin-Eater, then go around and claim drawbacks would be against theme. Or the reverse, but my point remains the same.<br /> <br /> I'd also note, that you can have downsides, and still find out what you got out a transaction is worth it. Or not, if that's how the person in question wants to look at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T16:57:48-07:00","id":978722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=978496#post978496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really get where the argument that Geist is <i>the </i>game about not being angsty came from.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mood section of 1e geist?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The protagonists are alive; they\u2019ve been given a second chance and the ability to experience the worlds of both living and dead. And like many people around the world, in this age and every other, they look on the specter of mortality and laugh. Eat, drink and be merry, as the adage goes, for tomorrow you may die. Geist is informed by Dia de los Muertos and Carnivale, by Halloween festivals and solstice fires.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does say not all sin-eaters follow the non-angsty-ness, but non-angsty-ness is the default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T07:16:44-07:00","id":978999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=978722#post978722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mood section of 1e geist?<br /> <br /> <br /> It does say not all sin-eaters follow the non-angsty-ness, but non-angsty-ness is the default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that isn't because they <i>don't</i> have anything to angst/worry about, but more that they <i>choose</i> not to. Halloween and Dia de los Muertos aren't celebrations of &quot;nothing to fear&quot;, they are celebrations <i>in defiance</i> of something to fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T07:33:13-07:00","id":979009,"title":"","content":"It's a game about coming back from the dead, it would be wrong to say that there is any one mood to capture it, it's all about ambivalence. There will be people who will treat their second chance at life as the best thing ever, a burden, a responsibility, or with apathy. It's an always changing mood that is completely reliant on the characters themselves and their environment (their geist, their setting, the ghosts and stories they deal with). Fate gave them a second chance and the power to make things different, it's ultimately their choice what to do with it. Someone can be changed from the event and squander it by becoming a crazy cat lady that never leaves their house for fear of dying again or try to be active and use newfound powers to better life for themselves and those they love.<br /> <br /> Life is like a box of chocolates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5557,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","user":"Runcible","date":". 09-30-2016, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T01:39:54-07:00","id":994463,"title":"","content":"I've been reading this and just wanted to share my thoughts, since there seems to be quite a bit of contention in terms of what people want for the sin-eater condition, particularly the relationship between Sin-Eater and Geist.<br /> <br /> Let me start off by saying that Geist was the first tabletop RPG I've ever encountered, so it will always have a very special place in my heart. That also means that I didn't know better when it came to Geists flaws. There are indeed a lot of them, and while I don't agree with some of the issues people have, I definitely agree that the Geist needs more teeth. As it is, they really don't have anything to do and it's not hard to ignore them out of game. That being said, one thing I absolutely agree with is that one of the appeals of Geist is that, all told, it's pretty great to be a Sin-Eater. You died and came back with magical powers. It's meant to be upbeat and celebratory, providing a new spin on death as a theme. So I definitely don't want being a sin-eater to become something harsh and unpleasant, but with regards to the Geist, they do need more teeth, and Sin-eaters need more mechanical reason to...be sin-eaters.<br /> <br /> So I'll offer some ideas I've had in that respect, using the examples offered above to illustrate them. First off, the example of the red-hand killer being essentially sealed away by his sin-eater. That should be a totally viable option. It should be possible for a sin-eater to ignore their Geists wishes if they really wanted to. But, as many people have pointed out, it takes a lot of weight out of the Bargain if ignoring a Geist has no significant consequences. And honestly, it takes away from the accomplishment of it too. In the core book, it says that sin-eaters nod in respect to her, she's clearly considered something special for being able to do that. So the mechanics should show that.<br /> <br /> My thinking would be that totally ignoring a Geist should have some negative effects after a while. Whether some tilts or conditions, combined with whatever penalties low synergy would bring. Also, make t so that after your synergy drops to a certain point, you actually have to expend willpower, maybe even plasm, illustrating that yes, keeping this beings demands in check requires serious effort. Because shutting down the urges of a demanding, quasi-death deity should absolutely be HARD. It should be a heroic task. There should be a reason why, to bring up another example, the burning ladys sin-eater makes the effort to go see the forest fires every year, or the risk of burning down targets to cleanse them instead of just doing something easier or just ignoring those desires outright. But here's the thing; those conditions she keeps getting? resolving them gets her beats. Constantly losing willpower and plasm means she has to indulge her virtues and vices regularly. It means she has to help ghosts pass on and find potent cenotes to keep herself filled with plasm. These ideas show that not everyone could do what she does. It demonstrates that your Geist isn't just a passenger, but someone you need to acknowledge and appease, and it does so in a way that doesn't mean being a sin-eater in general sucks, though it could suck to be a sin-eater with a particularly harsh or demanding Geist. It means your character has to work even harder to just go about their days with an angry spirit screaming in their heads. But it also means the character is stronger for it. It forces them to become a better sin-eater, because otherwise they'll crumble under the strain. It means that there's way around it-either you compromise with your Geist, dealing with the dead to at least some degree, or you deny it and have to face the dead so you're strong enough to keep overcoming it, but either way you have to be a sin-eater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T01:04:22-07:00","id":995112,"title":"","content":"Hm, I could easily see an integrity system similar to Werewolf's being of use here. The lower side of the spectrum being the geist and the upper being the human who died. Go lower and you find interaction in the real world harder, go higher and you find it more difficult to traverse Avernian gates and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T07:47:42-07:00","id":995191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=995112#post995112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, I could easily see an integrity system similar to Werewolf's being of use here. The lower side of the spectrum being the geist and the upper being the human who died. Go lower and you find interaction in the real world harder, go higher and you find it more difficult to traverse Avernian gates and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. Or we could have two &quot;Integrity Replacements&quot; like Deviant is going to have: One for how well-adjusted the player is to their life as a Sin-Eater (high good, call it Acceptance), and one for how pissed-off the Geist is at them (Low good, call it Unrest). High Acceptance makes you better at dealing with the living and resisting outside control (including your Geist taking over); High acceptances makes your struggle for control more, but also makes you more dangerous in combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T01:43:01-07:00","id":995551,"title":"","content":"Vampire, werewolf, changeling, and hunter all have somewhat &quot;antagonist-focused&quot; second editions, what with the &quot;X Chronicle&quot; format, and I'd predict something like that for Geist, because one of the biggest complaints about first edition was there wasn't really that much motivation to do anything, or any really compelling threats or mysteries or overarching plots. So that's something I'm one hundred percent sure 2e is going to give us. Cthonians being the focus is something else I could definitely see, since they were something about first edition that didn't get much explanation but that people really were interested in. &quot;Cthonians are trying to invade earth and break the boundaries between life and death&quot; is a good, immediate threat that players can engage with, and it fills the same niche as the strix or the Idigam in that it's something you can easily leave out of your chronicle if you want, but it's also easy to use as the centerpiece of one. <br /> <br /> I'm hoping we get some nods to Mummy, because it gave us some neat underworld stuff. I know there's a lot of argument over including crossover stuff right in the corebook, but just a few mentions of how well the lines work together would be nice. Mummy introduced sapient ghosts, and I'm hoping Geist picks that up, maybe even giving us some player options in that vein. It would be really neat if there was a ritual to grant full sapience to a ghost, plus some mechanic for sapient ghosts having to constantly hang on to their identities or fade into the two-dimensional flanderized shades most ghosts are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T02:11:59-07:00","id":995557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=995551#post995551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping we get some nods to Mummy, because it gave us some neat underworld stuff. I know there's a lot of argument over including crossover stuff right in the corebook, but just a few mentions of how well the lines work together would be nice. Mummy introduced sapient ghosts, and I'm hoping Geist picks that up, maybe even giving us some player options in that vein. It would be really neat if there was a ritual to grant full sapience to a ghost, plus some mechanic for sapient ghosts having to constantly hang on to their identities or fade into the two-dimensional flanderized shades most ghosts are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sapient ghosts are already in 2e, rank 2 ghosts are sapient while rank 1 ghosts are the 1e style recordings. Which also means Sin-Eaters might be able to give rank 1 ghosts plasm to increase their rank to 2, since Bound could make ghosts sapient via their plasmic infusion ability. And some dev's have said that we already have all the rules required for playing Ghosts (which is sort of true, but not exactly).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-30-2016, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T08:55:22-07:00","id":996099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=995557#post995557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sapient ghosts are already in 2e, rank 2 ghosts are sapient while rank 1 ghosts are the 1e style recordings. Which also means Sin-Eaters might be able to give rank 1 ghosts plasm to increase their rank to 2, since Bound could make ghosts sapient via their plasmic infusion ability. And some dev's have said that we already have all the rules required for playing Ghosts (which is sort of true, but not exactly).</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth pointing out that it has been confirmed that although Rank 1 ghosts are stuck in the loop, they are sentient (if not sapient). They aren't JUST recordings, they are just stuck re-doing the same actions over and over again, experiencing the horror of it over and over again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:15:15-07:00","id":996262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=996099#post996099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Worth pointing out that it has been confirmed that although Rank 1 ghosts are stuck in the loop, they are sentient (if not sapient). They aren't JUST recordings, they are just stuck re-doing the same actions over and over again, experiencing the horror of it over and over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty strong incentive to let your Rank rise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:34:54-07:00","id":996268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=996262#post996262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a pretty strong incentive to let your Rank rise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is that confirmed to be possible outside the Underworld in 2e? I'm not sure its really a consious choice anyway, just what happens eventually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:40:29-07:00","id":996270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=996268#post996268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is that confirmed to be possible outside the Underworld in 2e? I'm not sure its really a consious choice anyway, just what happens eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's restricted to the Underworld for the most part, but it also involves going deeper into the Underworld and drinking from the rivers there. I don't have sources on hand, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:44:09-07:00","id":996273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=996268#post996268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is that confirmed to be possible outside the Underworld in 2e? I'm not sure its really a consious choice anyway, just what happens eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why you really want a bound to pump you full of plasm. Force your rank up even in the land of the living.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:52:35-07:00","id":996279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=996273#post996273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why you really want a bound to pump you full of plasm. Force your rank up even in the land of the living.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, yeah, but that's temporary in 1st ed, don't know about 2nd. I think it would be worse knowing it was gonna go back to just looping in a short while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T06:33:46-07:00","id":997106,"title":"","content":"I do wonder how Archetypes will turn out. At first glance, Archetypes seem closer to some of the alternate Anchor traits other templates have been getting - Dirge/Mask, Blood/Bone, and Mask/Mien to be precise. Then again, they fit nicely with the 'course of action' types of Y-splats such as Refinements, Agendas, and Hungers.<br /> <br /> Hmm... if &quot;Sin-eater&quot; is now the playable part of the category of supernaturals collectively known as the Bound, would it constrain some Archetypes? The term &quot;Sin-eater&quot; seems to imply that the 'good' Bound are about being mediums and psychopomps, but I can't see how some Archetypes such as Bonepicker would fit into that schema.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:28:07-07:00","id":997124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=997106#post997106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... if &quot;Sin-eater&quot; is now the playable part of the category of supernaturals collectively known as the Bound, would it constrain some Archetypes? The term &quot;Sin-eater&quot; seems to imply that the 'good' Bound are about being mediums and psychopomps, but I can't see how some Archetypes such as Bonepicker would fit into that schema.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sin-Eater and Bound already meant that in 1e, and those archetypes weren't considered an issue...<br /> <br /> I'm rather surprised that several people weren't aware that Sin-Eaters were just the name given to Bound who help ghosts pass on","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T16:46:27-07:00","id":997957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=996268#post996268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is that confirmed to be possible outside the Underworld in 2e? I'm not sure its really a consious choice anyway, just what happens eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly ghosts can go as far as rank 2 without setting foot in the Underworld. Going any higher requires going to the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T18:08:24-07:00","id":997990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=997957#post997957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I remember correctly ghosts can go as far as rank 2 without setting foot in the Underworld. Going any higher requires going to the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought but was they could start either rank 1 or 2, but any advancement had to be in the underworld. Even from rank 1 to 2, that's just from memory though so I could be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T18:44:30-07:00","id":998546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=997990#post997990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought but was they could start either rank 1 or 2, but any advancement had to be in the underworld. Even from rank 1 to 2, that's just from memory though so I could be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure honestly. I just know that rank 2 is the cap without going to the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T02:46:06-07:00","id":998668,"title":"","content":"They can't increase Rank at all outside the Underworld (or the intervention of say Mages). For reasons unknown some Ghosts simply come into the world as Rank 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T00:12:26-08:00","id":999603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=998668#post998668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can't increase Rank at all outside the Underworld (or the intervention of say Mages). For reasons unknown some Ghosts simply come into the world as Rank 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely unknown; it's generally tied to Integrity at the moment of death. There are occasional exceptions (and of course in-universe it's a little more ambiguous because people can't see their own character sheets), but the rule of thumb is if your Integrity is &lt; 7, you come back Rank 1, if it's 7-9 you come back Rank 2, and if it's 10 you don't leave a ghost at all; whether that means you just stop existing or go back into the wheel of reincarnation or skip the busted-ass Underworld altogether and pass on to the &quot;real&quot; afterlife is anybody's guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T00:55:45-08:00","id":999613,"title":"","content":"Hmm, and I was here suspecting that they'd be more related to the Conditions you get from breaking points - what with ghosts being ephemeral pieces and imprints left of the original soul. Basing it on Integrity makes just as much as sense, though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T17:30:05-08:00","id":1014529,"title":"","content":"This is kind of minor, more a specific mechanic issue than anything about a system overall, but I think the Curse Manifestations seem pretty OP as they are now. Physical and mental attacks that not only damage a person, but can follow them around for days after the Sin-Eater is gone? And which can either take effect immediately or on a trigger, so it can be used either in battle or to assassinate people and leave no trace of involvement. There are a few small limitations, yeah, but overall it's immensely powerful, enough so that I honestly prefer not to see it used in a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T12:40:40-08:00","id":1014888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1014529#post1014529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is kind of minor, more a specific mechanic issue than anything about a system overall, but I think the Curse Manifestations seem pretty OP as they are now. Physical and mental attacks that not only damage a person, but can follow them around for days after the Sin-Eater is gone? And which can either take effect immediately or on a trigger, so it can be used either in battle or to assassinate people and leave no trace of involvement. There are a few small limitations, yeah, but overall it's immensely powerful, enough so that I honestly prefer not to see it used in a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe you've seen how Nightmares work for Beasts yet.<br /> <br /> But I think Curs should be included in the new game, just as all of the manifestations/haunts we currently have should. Just in a different form, like how Changeling Contracts all got reworked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T13:43:21-08:00","id":1014934,"title":"","content":"I didn't mean not included in 2e, or even 1e; if Curse got reworked, I'd love to see it stick around. I meant in actual Geist games I play, I don't like seeing our characters use Curse because of how powerful it is.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I haven't worked my way through all the different chronicles yet x_x So many books.<br /> <br /> To me, using powers against other supernatural types might be one thing (<i>might</i> be), but then there are regular mortals and hunters as well. An SE with good enough curses could more or less decimate an entire hunter conspiracy and never be found out, just by stalking individual hunters, getting within 30 yards or so, and applying a curse that will only trigger later.<br /> <br /> ...Frankly, I'd like to see hunters get some negation powers. Kind of like True Faith mixed with Paradox - they're not supernatural themselves, but their awareness and rejection of the supernatural weakens supernatural beings in their presence. I think a system like that could be a lot of fun and put them on more even footing with the other chronicles. They don't see through illusions - the illusion just won't hold around them. Edit: But that is a total tangent straying from Geist &gt;&gt; just a thought I thought I'd put out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T16:39:28-08:00","id":1015004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1014934#post1014934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, using powers against other supernatural types might be one thing (<i>might</i> be), but then there are regular mortals and hunters as well. An SE with good enough curses could more or less decimate an entire hunter conspiracy and never be found out, just by stalking individual hunters, getting within 30 yards or so, and applying a curse that will only trigger later.</div> </div> </div> </div>He wasn't suggesting using powers against other supernatural types. Nightmares function as curses you can put on people which you can decide to either activate now or activate in their sleep, meaning you can look someone in the eyes and then latter they turn to stone in their sleep with no evidence you were the cause. So it seems 2e CofD is fine with such mechanics (though of course you can still decide that you don't want that in your home games).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 12-09-2016, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T16:49:03-08:00","id":1015010,"title":"","content":"I know what he meant. What I meant is that giving different supernaturals the same level of power makes sense if you focus on having them potentially use those powers on each other, but when they're supposed to be a hidden minority in a population of weak, mundane mortals, it gets iffier for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T17:07:54-08:00","id":1015015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1015010#post1015010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know what he meant. What I meant is that giving different supernaturals the same level of power makes sense if you focus on having them potentially use those powers on each other, but when they're supposed to be a hidden minority in a population of weak, mundane mortals, it gets iffier for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't &quot;kill/damage/debilitate someone from kilometres away without evidence of you being the assailant&quot; help that not hinder that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T17:22:56-08:00","id":1015021,"title":"","content":"Not for me, but I like to experiment with a higher level of realism in my AR fantasy settings. If supernaturals are just <i>that</i> powerful, even against each other, it honestly begs the question why they have to hide from the weak little norms in the world, why they're not going around killing whoever they think needs killing, how they haven't been caught and revealed to the world yet. Or hell, even how they manage to keep information about themselves hidden from each other, since canonically most supernaturals don't know much about each other. This is all personal preference, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T17:52:54-08:00","id":1015036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1015021#post1015021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not for me, but I like to experiment with a higher level of realism in my AR fantasy settings. If supernaturals are just <i>that</i> powerful, even against each other, it honestly begs the question why they have to hide from the weak little norms in the world, why they're not going around killing whoever they think needs killing, how they haven't been caught and revealed to the world yet. Or hell, even how they manage to keep information about themselves hidden from each other, since canonically most supernaturals don't know much about each other. This is all personal preference, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the world is filled with <i>other</i> supernaturals that can do the same sort of thing, and even in a small niche like Sin Eaters are, they police themselves. Vampires regularly enforce the masquerade, Hunters are all about, Mages are essentially still human inside and may have a difference in opinion about someone going about messing things, the God-Machine has plans that it wouldn't like disrupted, as well as a vast number of Angels and Demons who are in their own phases of operation...really, openly going about and trying to do what you're describing is a terrible idea on all accounts because of how much attention it brings. Remember, a single supernatural may be potent, but they're literally going up against a world full of <i>pants-be-browning</i> things, both familiar and not.<br /> <br /> That's also ignoring the things normal humans can do when sufficiently incensed. Remember, humans have invented things like guns, nuclear weapons and <i>mustard gas</i>, and while not all of it would affect particular supernaturals, humanity has <i>something</i> in its repertoire that has some effect. Humanity has the advantage of numbers, resources and, in various quantities, stupidity. Never go against a fool with a blade, because with a master you know they'll be prepared. A fool doesn't know what they're doing and is as much a danger to themselves as everyone around them, including the person they're fighting.<br /> <br /> This is part of why supernaturals have powers like Curse and Nightmares. Those are the Guns they wield, just ones that work in more esoteric ways. Yes, against a normal human they're pretty damn dangerous...but that's <i>normal humans</i>. Against other supernaturals they're less likely to work, and that's why they have other powers that work at closer range. A normal person with a gun (such as a sniper rifle) fighting a normal person is more likely to succeed because of that very range advantage you're not liking, but on an even playing field it becomes less certain.<br /> <br /> Humanity in general is both the prey and the source of almost every supernatural in some way or another, and humanity is both looked down upon and coveted for the fact that they are normal.<br /> <br /> ...I came into this with a bit of a poor mood, so my post here is kind of angry and nonsensical. My apologies for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T17:53:55-08:00","id":1015037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1015021#post1015021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not for me, but I like to experiment with a higher level of realism in my AR fantasy settings. If supernaturals are just <i>that</i> powerful, even against each other, it honestly begs the question why they have to hide from the weak little norms in the world, why they're not going around killing whoever they think needs killing, how they haven't been caught and revealed to the world yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I think sin-eaters are past that point of power when they got the ability to survive being murdered multiple times in a single week, or being able to decide &quot;I'm fine&quot; after being shot in the head with a sniper rifle without even getting a scratch. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T20:29:44-08:00","id":1015142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1015021#post1015021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not for me, but I like to experiment with a higher level of realism in my AR fantasy settings. If supernaturals are just <i>that</i> powerful, even against each other, it honestly begs the question why they have to hide from the weak little norms in the world, why they're not going around killing whoever they think needs killing, how they haven't been caught and revealed to the world yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know what a blood oath is, Mr. Ness?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or hell, even how they manage to keep information about themselves hidden from each other, since canonically most supernaturals don't know much about each other. </div> </div> </div>Combination of global conspiracy and fact that the vast majority of their magic is at once metaphysically possessive and only fully comprehensible from inside the belly of the beast. If you can make sense of it it's because it's eating you while you're drinking its kool-aid.<br /> <br /> That's the epitome of unnecessary entanglement for most monsters, particularly when there's not that many of them when they aren't actively gathering together. Franklin the Fairest has enough on his plate getting to grips with being a changeling and living around the other changelings and assorted fairy bullshit that inhabit the same world as changelings, does he really have the time to spare learning the ins and outs of pack culture and spiritual etiquette instead of adding the dark alley by the gas-n-go and the weird dogs in the vacant lot to his list of Things To Avoid if the local werewolves aren't particularly involved with the local fae?<br /> <br /> Of course not. You keep your head down, you stay indoors, you cover your tracks, and above all else you don't take needless risks snooping around unknown quantities \u2014 mortal life prepared you for this even if existing in a framework where people on the lower end of conventional descriptions of gods walk around your municipality and occasionally give you a meaningful nod on a good day. The last thing most of the folks who manage to stick around want is a shake-up, so they keep to themselves and limit the level of cross-contamination to what they're prepared to risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T20:53:32-08:00","id":1017474,"title":"","content":"On another note, I'm sad Geist 2e is on the back burner in terms of which projects are getting prioritized, because I'm so eager to see how the writers will rework things like Synergy, the various merit and trait costs, etc. to fit with the 2e system. There might not be any huge changes in those areas, but it's still some little details I'd love to know.<br /> <br /> Synergy is particularly tricky, I think, because it doesn't only come from the character the way Integrity works for mortals; it comes from the bond between geist and Bound. The writers could do what they did in <i>Blood and Smoke</i> and just make some preset breaking points for each level of Synergy based on the geist side of the bargain. I imagine that's what they'll probably do. I'm not sure I like that idea, though, because although a geist and Bound are linked, they're still separate entities with their own minds. Synergy isn't about the Sin-Eater battling with their own sense of self - it's about their sense of self battling with their geist's sense of self.<br /> <br /> A character might face lowered Synergy by disregarding their geist's breaking points (banes?), but what if the geist tries to get them to disregard one of their own? GMC states that committing murder should always be considered a breaking point for a mortal, but death is what geists are all about. It might be interesting to see some sort of contested roll mechanic when one side is trying to influence the other against their own sense of Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":12708,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","user":"Chesh","date":". 12-15-2016, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T21:54:59-08:00","id":1017497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1017474#post1017474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, I'm sad Geist 2e is on the back burner in terms of which projects are getting prioritized, because I'm so eager to see how the writers will rework things like Synergy, the various merit and trait costs, etc. to fit with the 2e system. There might not be any huge changes in those areas, but it's still some little details I'd love to know.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't on the backburner, it's the next gameline to come out after Changeling 2e, and is currently being written (rather than Deviant or Hunter which are still being prepared by their developers).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Synergy is particularly tricky, I think, because it doesn't only come from the character the way Integrity works for mortals; it comes from the bond between geist and Bound. The writers could do what they did in <i>Blood and Smoke</i> and just make some preset breaking points for each level of Synergy based on the geist side of the bargain. I imagine that's what they'll probably do. I'm not sure I like that idea, though, because although a geist and Bound are linked, they're still separate entities with their own minds. Synergy isn't about the Sin-Eater battling with their own sense of self - it's about their sense of self battling with their geist's sense of self.<br /> <br /> A character might face lowered Synergy by disregarding their geist's breaking points (banes?), but what if the geist tries to get them to disregard one of their own? GMC states that committing murder should always be considered a breaking point for a mortal, but death is what geists are all about. It might be interesting to see some sort of contested roll mechanic when one side is trying to influence the other against their own sense of Integrity. </div> </div> </div>Synergy not working like Integrity is fine, most supernatural's &quot;integerity bar&quot; stats don't work like integrity. They will probably handle it in a manner similar to werewolf's harmony, which is about balacing your flesh-nature and your spirit-nature, but in this case it would represent the balance of power between Bound and Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 12-15-2016, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T22:17:02-08:00","id":1017504,"title":"","content":"Oh, sweet. Looking at the current projects for onyx path was discouraging because Geist seems pretty far off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T01:00:31-08:00","id":1017533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1017504#post1017504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, sweet. Looking at the current projects for onyx path was discouraging because Geist seems pretty far off.</div> </div> </div> </div>The current projects page is rather inaccurate, <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/news/monday-meeting/\" target=\"_blank\">monday meeting's</a> have more information on the status of projects. It's still pretty far off, but it takes time to create the second edition books. Changeling 2e started it's February 2015 and it's now in the development stage, probably ending up being released half-way through next year. Since geist only just got onto it's first draft very recently, it'll probably end up being released half-way through 2019.... So yeah..... It's not on the backburner, they're writing the 2e conversion of geist, but it's still ages away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 12-15-2016, 04:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T12:27:46-08:00","id":1028229,"title":"","content":"It's now 2017, and I can't help but wonder if we will see some blogs and spoilers for Geist 2E in the coming months, or (hopeful catch to my voice) sometime this month, especially with the possibility of a kickstarter coming up. I'm especially hopeful of a blog on the splats Geist 2E will use, a blog on Supporting Cast/Minor Template for Geist 2E, and a blog on Keys/Haunts in Gesit 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T13:50:25-08:00","id":1028256,"title":"","content":"I think a Changeling Kickstarter will happen first, but after that could I can see Geist next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T01:31:22-08:00","id":1028464,"title":"","content":"You know, I just had a thought; I apologize if I'm repeating anyone here, but what if the upcoming minor splat for Geist is an Abmortal? Abmortals are no longer specifically enemies, and they live by shunting death off of themselves, much like how a Geist can shunt death off of someone they have made the bargain with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T12:06:28-08:00","id":1033529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1028464#post1028464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I just had a thought; I apologize if I'm repeating anyone here, but what if the upcoming minor splat for Geist is an Abmortal? Abmortals are no longer specifically enemies, and they live by shunting death off of themselves, much like how a Geist can shunt death off of someone they have made the bargain with.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think its been said already that Abmortals is most likey reserved for other books period. <br /> <br /> Maybe the Mortal Splat is some kind of special Mediums, like people who were temporarily possessed by a Giest, but not bound and when the Giest left, it left the mortal changed into a Medium, sensitive to Bound and Ghosts. Just a guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T12:20:45-08:00","id":1033538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1033529#post1033529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think its been said already that Abmortals is most likey reserved for other books period.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Mortal Splat is some kind of special Mediums, like people who were temporarily possessed by a Giest, but not bound and when the Giest left, it left the mortal changed into a Medium, sensitive to Bound and Ghosts. Just a guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Whoopi Goldberg in Ghost?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://for