in &quot;it's&quot; body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 02-02-2017, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T20:24:58-08:00","id":1042776,"title":"","content":"Hmm sounds like my guess on the last page might be partially on the right track? On the note of a Sin-Eater dealing with its own ghost... what happens in the instance of a Sin-Eater that's been brought back more than once by its Geist, does it now have more than one ghost? or since it wasn't really brought up in 1e, what happens with the instance of the ghost of the person that had to die for your Geist to revive you? While it is mentioned the Sin-Eater views their death through their eyes before they wake up again, does that victim leave a vengeful ghost that knows some deathly powers were at work to slay them prematurely to bring you back? (Figure it could be a problem of being haunted by them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5557,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","user":"Runcible","date":". 02-02-2017, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T22:02:28-08:00","id":1042808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1042776#post1042776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm sounds like my guess on the last page might be partially on the right track? On the note of a Sin-Eater dealing with its own ghost... what happens in the instance of a Sin-Eater that's been brought back more than once by its Geist, does it now have more than one ghost? or since it wasn't really brought up in 1e, what happens with the instance of the ghost of the person that had to die for your Geist to revive you? While it is mentioned the Sin-Eater views their death through their eyes before they wake up again, does that victim leave a vengeful ghost that knows some deathly powers were at work to slay them prematurely to bring you back? (Figure it could be a problem of being haunted by them)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghost of the people who die in your place was my current theory for the new &quot;masked spectre&quot; antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T00:49:26-08:00","id":1042856,"title":"","content":"I was wondering if Dave wasn't hinting that it's the ghost making the bargain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T01:47:43-08:00","id":1042862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1042480#post1042480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's just awesome. Geist is awesome. This is the best thing ever. Being a person while not being a person, being alive, while still with one foot in the grave. Pure nihilism, which gives birth to the greatest celebration ever. Dancing with the dead in the carnival of life. So many images, so much beauty and tragedy and pain and hope and lust and shadows and light that its is just amazing. The gods of death being the trash of heaven, clinging to the cloths of pale horsemen as they ride toward the apocalypse and laugh all the way out. You are dead- but alive. You are a miracle, you are nothing. Who needs souls nowadays- not you. You just wear a mask instead and join the festival.</div> </div> </div> </div>Driving home that theme of &quot;people without souls are still <i>people</i>&quot; was one of the main reasons for the change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1042645#post1042645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A person dies and they become a ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily in that order. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":12259,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","user":"GimpInBlack","date":". 02-03-2017, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T06:05:47-08:00","id":1042896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1042856#post1042856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering if Dave wasn't hinting that it's the ghost making the bargain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah okay, well that's more along the lines of what I was thinking with my post before his. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:05:21-08:00","id":1043170,"title":"","content":"So the Giest makes a deal with your ghost, not your soul which left town, to bring your body back to life so your ghost and the Giest can experience life again.<br /> <br /> I look forward to the core book, I'm intrigued.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T04:48:58-08:00","id":1043476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1043170#post1043170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Giest makes a deal with your ghost, not your soul which left town, to bring your body back to life so your ghost and the Giest can experience life again.<br /> <br /> I look forward to the core book, I'm intrigued.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but teasers do not mean anything","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T08:41:00-08:00","id":1043575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1042645#post1042645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not all that die create a ghost, Just so that I know that I have this correct let me lay this out. A person dies and they become a ghost. If they have no anchors or their anchors are destroyed/resolved they are pulled into the Underworld where they can become a Geist. How fast can that happen? The Geist makes a Bargain with the Body of the dead, How recently dead, moment, Hours, Days, Weeks? How long does it take a rank 2 ghost to become a rank 3 Geist once in the Underworld. If the body can be dead for a while and the rank two Ghost can become a Rank 3 Geist fast enough I propose the scenario below.<br /> <br /> A person dies and they have no anchors then they immediately go to the underworld, become a Geist upon arrival and then make a deal with themselves to return a Sin-Eater. Their Ghost become Geist makes a deal with the Their dead body. The Bargain is Made and the Geist is no easier on his ex-body then he would be on a different body. Just a hypothetical and a possible character concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... the origin of Danny Phantom? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T11:40:09-08:00","id":1043655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1042645#post1042645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not all that die create a ghost, Just so that I know that I have this correct let me lay this out. A person dies and they become a ghost. If they have no anchors or their anchors are destroyed/resolved they are pulled into the Underworld where they can become a Geist. How fast can that happen? The Geist makes a Bargain with the Body of the dead, How recently dead, moment, Hours, Days, Weeks? How long does it take a rank 2 ghost to become a rank 3 Geist once in the Underworld. If the body can be dead for a while and the rank two Ghost can become a Rank 3 Geist fast enough I propose the scenario below.<br /> <br /> A person dies and they have no anchors then they immediately go to the underworld, become a Geist upon arrival and then make a deal with themselves to return a Sin-Eater. Their Ghost become Geist makes a deal with the Their dead body. The Bargain is Made and the Geist is no easier on his ex-body then he would be on a different body. Just a hypothetical and a possible character concept.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, ghosts don't become Giests when they get pulled into the underworld, they become Giests when they chose to drink from the rivers of the underworld, becoming rank 3 and embodying a concept of death. <br /> <br /> Before that they are just rank 1 and 2 ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T11:50:55-08:00","id":1043660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1043170#post1043170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Giest makes a deal with your ghost, not your soul which left town, to bring your body back to life so your ghost and the Giest can experience life again.<br /> <br /> I look forward to the core book, I'm intrigued.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that is the case, would that not arguably make Sin-Eaters something like Hive-Claimed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T12:12:38-08:00","id":1043672,"title":"","content":"Not quite, since claiming and bargaining are two different sets of powers. Also mentioned that a supplement book in the future would cover the concept a Geist Hive-Bargained, for lack of a better word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T22:16:37-08:00","id":1043862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1042480#post1042480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wait- what? who? when? what?! <b><i>what???</i></b><br /> <br /> that just caught me 100% off guard. Sin Eaters don't have souls. Sin. Eaters. Don't. Have. Souls. ha. haha. hahahahahaha. It's just so... so... so...<br /> <br /> its the craziest, weirdest, most appropriate thing I've ever heard. It's just so... right. All the internet arguments people had over whether or not <i>ghosts</i> should have souls, and that even without souls ghosts are still people- and now, this.<br /> <br /> Sin Eaters don't have souls.<br /> <br /> That's just awesome. Geist is awesome. This is the best thing ever. Being a person while not being a person, being alive, while still with one foot in the grave. Pure nihilism, which gives birth to the greatest celebration ever. Dancing with the dead in the carnival of life. So many images, so much beauty and tragedy and pain and hope and lust and shadows and light that its is just amazing. The gods of death being the trash of heaven, clinging to the cloths of pale horsemen as they ride toward the apocalypse and laugh all the way out. You are dead- but alive. You are a miracle, you are nothing. Who needs souls nowadays- not you. You just wear a mask instead and join the festival.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry- my synesthesia all flared out because of that sentence, and I had to write it down. It's just that awesome. No matter what other changes Geist is going to have, I think that this little thing is the best one.<br /> <br /> Sin Eaters don't have souls.<br /> <br /> That's awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>..... Kindly excuse me while I explode on this one, too.<br /> <br /> Okay, <i>that</i> is one of the biggest changes I did not see coming for Geist 2E.<br /> <br /> It definitely amps up the wierdness factor for them when it comes to interactions with the other splats. Mages might be weirded out by this revelation, seeing as two Arcana deal in the manipulation of the soul. Mummies would lump them into the Lifeless category since the lack of a soul means no Pillars (unless the <i>Ka</i> and/or <i>Sheut</i> is substituted by the Geist himself). Changelings and Prometheans would be similarly disturbed, seeing as the former lost parts of their soul to the durance and the latter are trying to transmute one through their Pilgrimage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T01:51:57-08:00","id":1043890,"title":"","content":"Damn. What <i>would</i> a Promethean think of that? Here they are, craving a soul and a normal human existence, empty and lost. Then there are Sin-Eaters, who are also empty but not &quot;bothered much&quot; by it and who still get to enjoy all the benefits of life. I'm getting a whiff of potential resentment and conflict...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T04:54:11-08:00","id":1043922,"title":"","content":"Whenever I imagine Sin-Eaters in a crossover environment, I always end up imagining each of the Bound's geists having a persona that ties to the other splats. Sin-eaters who bargained with Longius, Lycaon, Oberon, Osiris, Ammut, Angels, and Nyx. Toying with the other splats mythology would probably be rather amusing to some of the non-sacrosanct bound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T05:26:52-08:00","id":1043930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1043890#post1043890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn. What <i>would</i> a Promethean think of that? Here they are, craving a soul and a normal human existence, empty and lost. Then there are Sin-Eaters, who are also empty but not &quot;bothered much&quot; by it and who still get to enjoy all the benefits of life. I'm getting a whiff of potential resentment and conflict...</div> </div> </div> </div>ironically, in order to get a New Dawn a Promethean has to die and drink from a River- meaning that in order to get a soul, Prometheans has to learn how to lose on. I wonder what Geists would think of the Created drinking from the Rivers like they did, especially since the first lose their humanity from the act and the later gain it from doing so. Perhaps we will get something about it from the Crossover Chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T05:23:49-08:00","id":1044451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1043922#post1043922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whenever I imagine Sin-Eaters in a crossover environment, I always end up imagining each of the Bound's geists having a persona that ties to the other splats. Sin-eaters who bargained with Longius, Lycaon, Oberon, Osiris, Ammut, Angels, and Nyx. Toying with the other splats mythology would probably be rather amusing to some of the non-sacrosanct bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah this is a great thought. I did not think of that...thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T08:40:42-07:00","id":1083987,"title":"","content":"Maybe for the Y-Splat, <b>Business</b> (as in Unfinished Business). Something drove the Bound to reject their own death, and taking up the Bargain. Could have been <u>Vengeance</u> (the desire to make someone pay, either for their death, or something prior), <u>Protection</u> (not letting death stop them from saving, protecting, or providing for someone/something), <u>Obligation</u> (something needing to be completed before the grave can have its say), or just sheer <u>Rejection</u> (refusal to accept that life is now beyond them, or that they can die).<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Threshold would be how they died, Business would be why they said No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T14:14:52-07:00","id":1084146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1083987#post1083987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe for the Y-Splat, <b>Business</b> (as in Unfinished Business). Something drove the Bound to reject their own death, and taking up the Bargain. Could have been <u>Vengeance</u> (the desire to make someone pay, either for their death, or something prior), <u>Protection</u> (not letting death stop them from saving, protecting, or providing for someone/something), <u>Obligation</u> (something needing to be completed before the grave can have its say), or just sheer <u>Rejection</u> (refusal to accept that life is now beyond them, or that they can die).<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Threshold would be how they died, Business would be why they said No.</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather like that idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T15:57:13-07:00","id":1084195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1083987#post1083987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe for the Y-Splat, <b>Business</b> (as in Unfinished Business). Something drove the Bound to reject their own death, and taking up the Bargain. Could have been <u>Vengeance</u> (the desire to make someone pay, either for their death, or something prior), <u>Protection</u> (not letting death stop them from saving, protecting, or providing for someone/something), <u>Obligation</u> (something needing to be completed before the grave can have its say), or just sheer <u>Rejection</u> (refusal to accept that life is now beyond them, or that they can die).<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Threshold would be how they died, Business would be why they said No.</div> </div> </div> </div>Issue with that would be that it means there is a very quick end point to the entire point of your Y-splat unless the whole campaign revolves around you. After two or three sessions it becomes worthless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T17:05:12-07:00","id":1084211,"title":"","content":"I have the same issue so I think this Business could use some work. That was my first thought. My second was how it would work out if the Business was related to the Geist. Much more play could be derived from Vengeance when the Sin-eater is largely unaware of the details. The Geist forgot the details and just tends to want to see vengeance dished out.<br /> <br /> I don't expect any open development, so I suspect the details are already worked out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T17:11:30-07:00","id":1084212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1084211#post1084211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the same issue so I think this Business could use some work. That was my first thought. My second was how it would work out if the Business was related to the Geist. Much more play could be derived from Vengeance when the Sin-eater is largely unaware of the details. The Geist forgot the details and just tends to want to see vengeance dished out.<br /> <br /> I don't expect any open development, so I suspect the details are already worked out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Y-Splat being specific to the nature of the Geist in the character is another interesting option. Perhaps, in that option, the Geist's outlook or approach to the Bargain is the Y-splat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T07:44:31-07:00","id":1084479,"title":"","content":"Wonder if there will also be an anthology book coming for this. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T13:35:43-07:00","id":1084675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1084479#post1084479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonder if there will also be an anthology book coming for this. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>My vote and hope is YES! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T18:13:53-07:00","id":1084794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1084479#post1084479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonder if there will also be an anthology book coming for this. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Thus far the 2E corebooks have had all anthologies, haven't they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T19:26:27-07:00","id":1084825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1084794#post1084794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thus far the 2E corebooks have had all anthologies, haven't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes indeed. God-Machine Chronicle Anthology, Strix Chronicle Anthology (Vampire Requiem), Idigam Chronicle Anthology (Werewolf Forsaken), Fallen World Chronicle Anthology (Mage Awakening), Firestorm Chronicle Anthology (Promethean Created), Interface Anthology (Demon Descent), Primordial Feast Anthology (Beast Primordial).<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen Chronicle Anthology (for the upcoming Changeling 2E) is currently at WWP for approvals according to the last Monday's Notes &amp; the Current Projects page specifically mentions a Slasher Chronicle Anthology (for the upcoming Hunter 2E).<br /> <br /> I'm positive there will be a Geist one in the works before long, especially as Geist 2E is further along on the development schedule than Hunter that already has one promised <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T07:26:28-07:00","id":1085016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=1084195#post1084195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Issue with that would be that it means there is a very quick end point to the entire point of your Y-splat unless the whole campaign revolves around you. After two or three sessions it becomes worthless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it could work if it becomes a general affinity you have to ghosts with similar unresolved issue and connected to powers that define your approach (offensive for vengeance, defensive for protection, etc). It could be a neat synergy with Threshold. Someone who drowned and came back for vengeance would have water-themed hurt-y, curse-y powers, where if the same person came back to protect someone their watery powers would be shrouds and barriers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}